WEBVTT

00:18.146 --> 00:20.349
[ominous music playing]

00:55.589 --> 00:57.584
[siren wailing]

01:38.258 --> 01:40.462
[indistinct chatter]

02:23.403 --> 02:24.902
I don't remember you.

02:25.878 --> 02:27.575
-Does it matter?
-No.

02:35.283 --> 02:37.387
Smart decision, Hoffman.

02:39.225 --> 02:43.855
I look at you,
and you seem almost normal.

02:45.391 --> 02:47.166
Arrogant but normal.

02:48.665 --> 02:52.171
I thought I'd get to see
what evil really looked like...

02:54.338 --> 02:56.637
but you just look like
everyone else.

02:58.339 --> 02:59.904
Is that it? Can I go now?

03:01.742 --> 03:04.076
This is everything
that I took from you.

03:04.746 --> 03:07.447
My representatives
will keep one safety copy.

03:07.549 --> 03:10.282
If your thugs
follow me out of here,

03:10.384 --> 03:12.550
if anything happens to me,

03:12.652 --> 03:14.924
that copy
goes to law enforcement--

03:15.026 --> 03:17.361
I know how this works.

03:26.807 --> 03:28.207
I need to take a picture.

03:29.774 --> 03:30.869
Of us.

03:37.444 --> 03:39.383
[McVie] Two old buddies.

03:40.786 --> 03:41.818
[shutter clicks]

03:41.920 --> 03:43.222
Hope you frame it.

03:44.617 --> 03:46.753
Good luck with your new life,

03:47.925 --> 03:49.426
Mr. Hoffman.

03:56.530 --> 03:58.765
[suspenseful music playing]

04:37.142 --> 04:39.344
[suspenseful music continues]

04:46.985 --> 04:48.316
Thanks for waiting.

04:48.652 --> 04:51.323
Uptown, please.
I'll tell you where in a minute.

04:55.061 --> 04:57.296
[suspenseful music continues]

05:00.799 --> 05:02.961
[beeping]

05:19.746 --> 05:21.980
[suspenseful music intensifies]

05:53.946 --> 05:55.948
[woman speaking indistinctly
over PA]

06:01.289 --> 06:03.054
[bell rings]

06:45.871 --> 06:47.838
[tapping]

06:47.940 --> 06:48.840
[door buzzes]

06:48.942 --> 06:50.937
[music fades out]

06:54.674 --> 06:56.844
[elevator bell dings]

07:01.187 --> 07:03.180
[indistinct chatter nearby]

07:07.292 --> 07:09.494
[soft dramatic music playing]

07:24.911 --> 07:26.578
[line ringing]

07:26.680 --> 07:30.310
[automated voice]<i> Special</i>
<i> answering service, inbox 482.</i>

07:30.412 --> 07:31.778
<i> One new message.</i>

07:31.880 --> 07:33.383
[McVie on message]
<i> We have the report back.</i>

07:33.485 --> 07:35.183
<i> You've been paid</i>
<i> for your services.</i>

07:35.285 --> 07:36.585
<i> As long as Hoffman</i>

07:36.688 --> 07:38.686
<i>sticks to his side of the deal,</i>
<i> we're done.</i>

07:38.788 --> 07:41.693
<i> And by the way,</i>
<i> a message from my boss.</i>

07:42.095 --> 07:44.056
<i> You're parasitic scum.</i>

07:45.394 --> 07:46.861
[voice mail beeps]

07:52.906 --> 07:54.935
[squeaking]

07:59.077 --> 08:01.106
[train rumbling]

08:20.427 --> 08:21.863
[beeping]

08:23.465 --> 08:24.569
[digital lock beeps]

08:39.419 --> 08:41.245
-[voice mail beeps]
<i> -Hoffman here.</i>

08:41.347 --> 08:44.314
<i> He showed last night.</i>
<i> I handed over the documents</i>

08:44.416 --> 08:47.490
<i> and took the train</i>
<i> to Poughkeepsie as instructed.</i>

08:47.592 --> 08:49.119
<i> I hope the safety copy</i>
<i> is enough</i>

08:49.221 --> 08:52.558
<i> to keep Optimo off my back</i>
<i> and yours.</i>

08:52.993 --> 08:54.429
<i> I sent the other half</i>
<i> of the money</i>

08:54.531 --> 08:56.265
<i> to the address you provided.</i>

08:56.601 --> 08:58.536
<i> I wasn't expecting</i>
<i> so much myself.</i>

08:58.638 --> 09:01.865
<i> I thought that would go</i>
<i> for your fee. Thank you.</i>

09:01.967 --> 09:04.169
[train rumbling in distance]

09:06.345 --> 09:07.843
<i> Are they gonna play fair?</i>

09:08.543 --> 09:09.548
[voice mail beeps]

09:14.987 --> 09:16.984
[beeping]

09:24.931 --> 09:25.729
[clicks]

09:30.202 --> 09:32.230
[train horn blares]

09:43.380 --> 09:45.584
[flames crackling]

09:48.617 --> 09:50.820
[somber music playing]

10:17.381 --> 10:18.246
[woman] Ms. Grant?

10:18.348 --> 10:19.581
Hi. I'm Julie.

10:19.683 --> 10:21.116
-Hi.
-Mr. Morel will see you now.

10:21.219 --> 10:22.346
Thank you.

10:25.191 --> 10:25.990
[clears throat]

10:26.092 --> 10:27.424
I was in a team,

10:27.526 --> 10:28.919
uh, developing
a new wheat strain

10:29.021 --> 10:30.459
resistant to insect predation

10:30.561 --> 10:32.261
through precision breeding.

10:32.730 --> 10:36.093
It's... It's like
genetic modification,

10:36.195 --> 10:37.801
only it's using
natural processes,

10:37.903 --> 10:41.136
so it's not subject
to the same tight regulation.

10:41.238 --> 10:42.367
Anyway.

10:42.803 --> 10:44.269
We were making progress,

10:44.371 --> 10:48.777
but we were noticing possible
human food-chain issues.

10:48.879 --> 10:51.310
Um, and then I was CC'ed
on an e-mail chain

10:51.412 --> 10:53.781
where one of the attachments
was a food safety assessment

10:53.883 --> 10:56.419
showing significant
side effects.

10:56.888 --> 10:58.855
When I raised this issue
with senior management,

10:58.957 --> 11:02.093
um, they told me that
I'd seen the data out of context

11:02.195 --> 11:03.791
and not to worry.

11:03.893 --> 11:06.190
But then, um,
soon, I was transferred

11:06.292 --> 11:08.827
to another department
here in Manhattan.

11:08.929 --> 11:10.862
Office work, data assessment.

11:10.965 --> 11:13.704
Um, and then, two months later,

11:13.806 --> 11:15.872
I was dismissed
on a minor time card violation,

11:15.974 --> 11:19.975
and now I'm being subjected
to escalating harassment.

11:20.442 --> 11:21.574
Uh...

11:22.010 --> 11:23.777
I'm sorry to hear that,
Ms. Grant.

11:23.879 --> 11:25.915
Why do you think
this is happening?

11:26.515 --> 11:28.152
I felt, um...

11:28.621 --> 11:30.181
Well, I felt I had a duty
to take a copy

11:30.283 --> 11:34.124
of the food safety assessment
as evidence.

11:34.893 --> 11:37.790
You stole documents
from your former employers?

11:37.892 --> 11:41.161
Is that... Is that stealing?

11:43.330 --> 11:47.203
May I ask why you decided
to discuss this issue

11:47.305 --> 11:49.370
with our firm?

11:49.739 --> 11:51.974
I followed a recommendation.

11:52.707 --> 11:54.575
May I ask from whom?

11:55.111 --> 11:58.783
A friend. It wouldn't be
appropriate to say who.

12:02.921 --> 12:05.383
Ms. Grant, I commend you
on your intentions here,

12:05.485 --> 12:08.857
but we're no longer looking
for this type of business.

12:08.959 --> 12:11.991
Uh, there are a number
of highly regarded

12:12.093 --> 12:13.660
whistleblower
support organizations

12:13.762 --> 12:15.259
much better prepared--

12:15.361 --> 12:17.564
No. It's not
whistleblowing support I need.

12:17.666 --> 12:19.100
It's the opposite.

12:21.234 --> 12:23.303
I just want
to give everything back

12:23.405 --> 12:27.607
and promise to keep my mouth
shut and get on with my life.

12:27.709 --> 12:29.147
[whimpers softly]

12:29.249 --> 12:31.849
Please. Please.

12:33.486 --> 12:35.484
Is there anyone who can help me?

12:35.586 --> 12:37.756
[somber music playing]

12:39.993 --> 12:44.059
Well, as I said, there are
official channels, but, uh...

12:47.596 --> 12:49.130
Look, um...

12:49.930 --> 12:51.536
There are unofficial ones

12:51.638 --> 12:53.838
we've referred people to
in the past.

12:57.174 --> 13:01.144
Just take this number,
and maybe they can help you.

13:01.247 --> 13:02.376
[sniffles]

13:02.945 --> 13:05.348
-Who is he?
-I've never met him,

13:05.450 --> 13:07.444
or her or they.

13:07.546 --> 13:10.482
That's kind of the point.
It's a messaging service.

13:10.951 --> 13:12.890
They call you back...

13:13.523 --> 13:14.818
or they don't.

13:15.387 --> 13:18.956
Just be honest
about your situation.

13:19.058 --> 13:21.294
[somber music continues]

13:30.674 --> 13:32.877
[somber music continues]

13:42.787 --> 13:44.988
-[alarm beeping]
-[music fades out]

13:49.221 --> 13:51.456
[train horn blaring in distance]

14:01.406 --> 14:02.335
[car horn honks]

14:08.578 --> 14:09.845
You are all set.

14:09.947 --> 14:12.042
The lobby's attended
24 hours a day.

14:12.144 --> 14:13.310
Call if you need anything.

14:13.412 --> 14:15.179
Thanks for doing this
on short notice.

14:15.281 --> 14:17.515
That's what we do.
Enjoy your stay.

14:21.723 --> 14:22.889
[door closes]

14:22.991 --> 14:24.621
[suspenseful music playing]

14:46.819 --> 14:49.387
Hey, I'm Wash,
and I'm an alcoholic.

14:49.489 --> 14:51.351
-Hi, Wash.
-Hi, Wash.

14:52.225 --> 14:53.353
Um...

14:55.092 --> 14:57.654
I've been sober nine years,
nine months.

14:59.595 --> 15:01.031
And...

15:02.033 --> 15:05.265
It's been even more
of a struggle recently

15:05.367 --> 15:08.871
because there's
why I drank in the first place,

15:08.973 --> 15:13.309
and then there's me
doing what I do.

15:13.945 --> 15:16.145
'Cause I'm proud
of serving on the force.

15:17.078 --> 15:18.950
And I stay on the up and up.

15:20.553 --> 15:22.219
Pretty much. [chuckles]

15:22.322 --> 15:23.350
But, um...

15:25.619 --> 15:29.592
What I see on the daily,
amongst my fellow officers...

15:29.694 --> 15:31.358
I... I... I don't know.

15:34.263 --> 15:36.462
[indistinct chatter
and laughter nearby]

15:43.238 --> 15:44.934
[automated voice]
<i> Two new messages.</i>

15:45.537 --> 15:48.346
[on message]
<i> Hoffman here. All right.</i>

15:48.448 --> 15:49.813
[voice mail beeps]

15:49.915 --> 15:51.610
[on message]
<i> My name is Sarah Grant.</i>

15:51.712 --> 15:54.616
<i> Um, I was a scientist</i>
<i> working at a biotech company,</i>

15:54.718 --> 15:56.281
<i> Cybo Sementis.</i>

15:56.383 --> 15:59.186
<i> I... I'm in possession</i>
<i> of materials</i>

15:59.289 --> 16:02.153
<i> which are evidence</i>
<i> of an unlawful cover-up.</i>

16:02.622 --> 16:05.662
<i> I was gonna go public,</i>
<i> but I changed my mind.</i>

16:05.764 --> 16:07.160
<i> I don't know how this works,</i>

16:07.262 --> 16:09.630
<i> but I'll do</i>
<i> whatever is necessary.</i>

16:09.999 --> 16:16.436
<i> My number is 693-824-4011.</i>

16:18.137 --> 16:19.642
[voice mail beeps]

16:19.744 --> 16:21.738
[pensive music playing]

16:44.736 --> 16:46.697
[keyboard keys clacking]

16:57.683 --> 17:00.579
<i> ♪ If you felt alive ♪</i>

17:01.984 --> 17:05.353
<i> ♪ I couldn't tell ♪</i>

17:06.989 --> 17:11.562
<i> ♪ I couldn't tell ♪</i>

17:11.664 --> 17:15.892
<i> ♪ I couldn't tell ♪</i>

17:16.461 --> 17:19.136
<i> ♪ It's coming to an end ♪</i>

17:21.674 --> 17:23.907
<i> ♪ The world is now ♪</i>

17:24.009 --> 17:26.203
<i> We are delighted</i>
<i> to be the recipients</i>

17:26.305 --> 17:28.074
<i> of the Lansing Award.</i>

17:28.176 --> 17:30.241
<i>This research has the potential</i>

17:30.344 --> 17:32.249
<i> to revolutionize grain yields,</i>

17:32.351 --> 17:35.116
<i> particularly in developing</i>
<i> countries, where they need it,</i>

17:35.218 --> 17:36.983
<i> lowering reliance</i>
<i> on pesticides.</i>

17:37.085 --> 17:38.890
<i> And with this grant,</i>

17:38.992 --> 17:41.086
<i> we really hope</i>
<i> to make a difference.</i>

17:41.188 --> 17:43.688
<i> ♪ Far from this place ♪</i>

17:45.291 --> 17:48.059
<i> ♪ A brand-new way... ♪</i>

17:48.161 --> 17:50.365
[cellphone ringing]

17:56.572 --> 17:58.975
[operator]<i> Hello. This is</i>
<i> the Tri-State Relay Service.</i>

17:59.077 --> 18:00.707
-Yes. Hello.
<i> -A person is calling</i>

18:00.809 --> 18:03.510
<i>through relay service. Have you</i>
<i> received a relay call before?</i>

18:03.612 --> 18:06.280
<i> -I don't think so.</i>
-The person who has called you

18:06.382 --> 18:08.348
is likely to be deaf
or hard of hearing.

18:08.450 --> 18:09.884
The caller will type
their conversation,

18:09.986 --> 18:11.386
and I'll read it to you.

18:11.488 --> 18:14.224
When it's your turn,
I'll type everything you say.

18:14.326 --> 18:16.894
<i> Speak directly to the caller</i>
<i> and say, "Go ahead,"</i>

18:16.996 --> 18:18.359
<i> when you're ready</i>
<i> for a response.</i>

18:18.461 --> 18:20.464
<i> No calls are recorded,</i>
<i> and everything you say</i>

18:20.566 --> 18:22.059
is confidential.

18:22.595 --> 18:24.630
One moment
for your call to begin.

18:25.365 --> 18:26.730
<i>"You are Sarah Elizabeth Grant.</i>

18:26.832 --> 18:31.135
<i> Your Social Security number</i>
<i> is 958-00-4493."</i>

18:31.237 --> 18:33.474
[teletype beeping]

18:36.074 --> 18:38.776
<i> "You were employed by Cybo</i>
<i> Sementis Research Institutes,</i>

18:38.878 --> 18:45.718
tax ID 99-0890590, based
in St. Louis. Is that correct?"

18:45.820 --> 18:47.323
Yes.

18:48.689 --> 18:50.456
<i> If finished,</i>
<i>please respond with "Go ahead."</i>

18:50.559 --> 18:53.291
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
I'm sorry. Go ahead.

18:53.393 --> 18:56.596
"Please explain your situation."

18:58.837 --> 19:00.402
I was in a research group

19:00.504 --> 19:05.342
developing a new strain
of insect-resistant wheat.

19:05.945 --> 19:07.979
Um, a food-safety report
came back

19:08.081 --> 19:10.643
with disturbing data
about side effects.

19:11.618 --> 19:13.346
I told my bosses.

19:13.448 --> 19:15.682
Next thing I knew,
I'd been reassigned

19:16.117 --> 19:18.315
and later dismissed.

19:18.818 --> 19:20.552
Production of the new strain
has gone ahead,

19:20.654 --> 19:23.189
but these findings
have been suppressed.

19:23.792 --> 19:28.632
Um, but I was able to get a copy
of that food safety report

19:28.734 --> 19:29.893
out of the building.

19:31.636 --> 19:32.566
Go ahead.

19:40.242 --> 19:41.806
"You mention side effects."

19:42.508 --> 19:45.049
In a small number of cases,

19:45.151 --> 19:49.415
there were extreme allergies,
anaphylaxis.

19:49.517 --> 19:52.451
And in longer-term cases,
diverticulitis

19:52.553 --> 19:55.685
<i> and cancer</i>
<i> well above base rate.</i>

19:55.787 --> 19:58.589
They project
massive worldwide sales.

19:58.691 --> 20:01.262
Thousands of people
will be affected.

20:01.364 --> 20:02.593
But without
the information I have,

20:02.695 --> 20:04.362
it will be impossible
to trace it back

20:04.464 --> 20:06.131
to the food people have eaten.

20:06.233 --> 20:08.404
[teletype beeping]

20:09.139 --> 20:10.338
<i> "Would you say this document</i>

20:10.440 --> 20:12.673
<i> contains clear evidence</i>
<i> of malfeasance?"</i>

20:12.775 --> 20:17.811
Compared to the fraudulent
version of their report, yes.

20:17.913 --> 20:18.981
Go ahead.

20:19.383 --> 20:20.851
<i> "Did they offer you</i>
<i> a cash settlement</i>

20:20.954 --> 20:22.548
<i> in exchange for your silence?"</i>

20:22.650 --> 20:25.817
Um, initially, yes,
but I wasn't interested.

20:27.653 --> 20:29.788
I wanted to do the right thing.

20:31.096 --> 20:34.632
But then
the intimidation started.

20:34.734 --> 20:36.897
[teletype beeping]

20:37.433 --> 20:40.768
Last night,
they set my car on fire.

20:40.870 --> 20:42.273
Go ahead.

20:43.239 --> 20:44.701
<i> "Are the police involved?"</i>

20:44.803 --> 20:46.272
They towed the car away
as evidence,

20:46.374 --> 20:48.713
but I haven't involved them.

20:48.815 --> 20:51.412
<i> -Go ahead.</i>
-"Don't.

20:51.515 --> 20:54.582
<i>Was this at 200 Chambers Street</i>
<i> in Tribeca?"</i>

20:55.686 --> 20:56.918
Yes.

20:57.520 --> 21:00.786
But I've moved now
because of the threats.

21:02.354 --> 21:03.728
<i> Go ahead.</i>

21:03.830 --> 21:05.824
[keyboard keys clacking]

21:06.492 --> 21:08.328
"Buy a prepaid cellphone,

21:08.764 --> 21:11.432
keep it switched off
till you get to a public place,

21:11.534 --> 21:13.401
then leave a message
with your new number,

21:13.503 --> 21:17.308
<i> new address,</i>
<i> and any further details."</i>

21:18.572 --> 21:21.210
There's a van parked out front.

21:21.312 --> 21:24.315
I think they're watching me.
Go ahead.

21:26.348 --> 21:28.545
<i>"They may be tapping this call.</i>

21:28.915 --> 21:31.414
<i> In the future,</i>
<i> only use your new phone."</i>

21:31.516 --> 21:32.916
[disconnect sound]

21:33.018 --> 21:34.754
<i> Your caller has hung up.</i>
<i> Thank you for using</i>

21:34.856 --> 21:37.559
<i> the Tri-State Relay Service.</i>
<i> Have a wonderful night.</i>

21:45.636 --> 21:48.172
[Sarah on recording]
<i>There's a van parked out front.</i>

21:48.274 --> 21:50.438
<i> I think they're watching me.</i>
<i> Go ahead.</i>

21:50.540 --> 21:54.708
Okay. 339 East Avenue,
Yonkers, New York.

21:54.810 --> 21:56.539
[operator on recording]
<i> "Only use your new phone."</i>

21:56.641 --> 21:59.080
Night shift. Who's coming?

21:59.182 --> 22:01.385
[soft tense music playing]

22:31.617 --> 22:35.386
The Americans with Disabilities
Act of 1990, Section 225,

22:35.488 --> 22:37.416
prohibits relay operators
from disclosing the content

22:37.518 --> 22:39.618
of any relayed conversation

22:39.720 --> 22:41.458
and from keeping records
of the content

22:41.560 --> 22:44.159
of any such conversation
beyond the duration of the call.

22:44.261 --> 22:46.193
Okay. Okay. I don't want to go

22:46.295 --> 22:47.461
and get a warrant. Do you?

22:47.563 --> 22:49.926
-No.
-Where'd you say you're from?

22:50.028 --> 22:52.500
-Treasury Department.
-Misappropriations.

22:52.869 --> 22:55.865
Okay. Even with a warrant,
there'd be nothing to search.

22:55.967 --> 22:57.804
We don't keep
records of our logs,

22:57.906 --> 23:00.543
where they're coming from,
or where they're going to.

23:03.880 --> 23:05.141
Mm.

23:07.216 --> 23:08.316
This is Sarah Grant.

23:08.418 --> 23:14.490
Um, my new number
is 718-493-7071.

23:14.592 --> 23:20.457
1500 Washington Street,
apartment 2Q, uh, 10006.

23:21.359 --> 23:25.467
[clears throat] The company is
on the verge of being acquired

23:25.569 --> 23:29.440
based on an estimated value
of $3.2 billion,

23:29.542 --> 23:31.769
which will be confirmed
at an SEC filing next week.

23:31.871 --> 23:34.473
<i> If the information I had</i>
<i> went public,</i>

23:34.575 --> 23:35.907
<i> it would break that deal.</i>

23:36.009 --> 23:37.948
<i> They are highly incentivized</i>
<i> to prevent that,</i>

23:38.050 --> 23:39.411
<i> which is why I'm scared.</i>

23:39.513 --> 23:42.420
[dramatic music playing]

24:08.277 --> 24:10.514
[indistinct chatter]

24:12.577 --> 24:15.178
[siren whooping]

24:24.391 --> 24:25.958
[car horn honks]

24:29.034 --> 24:30.501
[car horns honking]

24:39.076 --> 24:40.038
[door buzzes]

24:43.675 --> 24:45.078
[cellphone rings]

24:45.614 --> 24:47.311
-Hello.
-A person is calling you

24:47.413 --> 24:50.183
through Relay Service. Have you
received a relay call before?

24:50.285 --> 24:51.918
Yes. Go ahead.

24:53.120 --> 24:56.458
<i> "After reviewing your</i>
<i> situation, here's the deal.</i>

24:56.560 --> 24:57.989
<i> We can help you</i>
<i> return the documents</i>

24:58.091 --> 25:00.991
<i> whilst maintaining leverage</i>
<i> to protect you.</i>

25:01.093 --> 25:04.095
<i> We require</i>
<i> a $50,000 deposit up front.</i>

25:04.197 --> 25:06.433
<i> This will be returned to you</i>
<i> from money we recover</i>

25:06.535 --> 25:08.566
<i>during the negotiation process.</i>

25:08.668 --> 25:10.104
<i> Can you afford this?"</i>

25:10.206 --> 25:12.171
Yes. Go ahead.

25:12.540 --> 25:13.905
<i> "Over the next few days,</i>

25:14.007 --> 25:15.776
<i> you will receive</i>
<i> some strange requests</i>

25:15.878 --> 25:17.812
<i> designed to show us</i>
<i> what we're up against.</i>

25:17.914 --> 25:21.352
<i> Please follow all instructions</i>
<i> no matter how odd.</i>

25:21.454 --> 25:23.120
<i> In the future,</i>
<i> we will use a passcode</i>

25:23.222 --> 25:24.286
<i> before each conversation.</i>

25:24.389 --> 25:26.419
We will say, 'Credit or debit?'

25:26.521 --> 25:27.685
You will say, 'Check.'

25:27.788 --> 25:30.457
<i> -Understood?"</i>
-Understood.

25:30.559 --> 25:32.761
[suspenseful music playing]

25:53.747 --> 25:55.982
[vehicle backup alarm beeping]

25:58.290 --> 26:00.283
[suspenseful music continues]

26:06.558 --> 26:08.093
[buzzing]

26:12.697 --> 26:13.631
Who is it?

26:13.733 --> 26:15.166
[man]<i> Package for you.</i>

26:35.987 --> 26:38.222
[suspenseful music continues]

26:43.364 --> 26:44.327
Thanks.

27:00.383 --> 27:02.620
[cellphone ringing]

27:05.722 --> 27:07.721
-Hello.
<i> -Tri-State Relay Service.</i>

27:07.823 --> 27:09.488
Have you received
a relay call before?

27:09.590 --> 27:10.423
<i> Yes. Go ahead.</i>

27:10.525 --> 27:12.061
<i> Credit or debit?</i>

27:12.163 --> 27:13.156
Check. Go ahead.

27:13.258 --> 27:15.759
"Tomorrow morning,
take the 10:05 flight

27:15.861 --> 27:16.959
from Newark to Pittsburgh,

27:17.061 --> 27:19.698
<i> then the 11:50 to Atlanta.</i>

27:19.800 --> 27:21.768
Do not take this phone with you.

27:21.870 --> 27:23.773
<i> Take the packages</i>
<i> with our deposit</i>

27:23.875 --> 27:26.238
<i> and the report and the</i>
<i>red-marked phone you were sent.</i>

27:26.340 --> 27:30.043
<i>Do not turn it on until you are</i>
<i> at your gate in Pittsburgh."</i>

27:31.646 --> 27:32.711
Your caller has hung up.

27:32.813 --> 27:35.052
Operator, I forgot something.

27:35.154 --> 27:36.685
<i> Can I call back?</i>

27:36.788 --> 27:39.355
The caller has placed
a no-callback request

27:39.457 --> 27:41.923
<i> on this line. Sorry, ma'am.</i>

27:45.929 --> 27:48.165
-[indistinct chatter]
-[plane passing overhead]

27:48.267 --> 27:50.261
[dramatic music playing]

27:59.408 --> 28:00.678
[woman] Next.

28:37.813 --> 28:40.784
[man speaking indistinctly
over PA]

28:57.129 --> 28:59.462
-Thank you.
-Thank you so much.

29:01.766 --> 29:03.103
Hello.

29:07.907 --> 29:09.076
[barcode scanner beeps]

29:20.222 --> 29:22.117
[woman over PA]<i> This is</i>
<i> a preboarding announcement</i>

29:22.219 --> 29:24.990
<i> for Flight 8917 to Atlanta.</i>

29:25.092 --> 29:26.894
<i> We are expecting</i>
<i> a full flight today,</i>

29:26.996 --> 29:28.794
<i> so if you'd like</i>
<i> to gate-check your bag,</i>

29:28.896 --> 29:30.663
<i> please see us at the desk.</i>

29:30.765 --> 29:32.968
[dramatic music continues]

29:45.350 --> 29:46.443
[cellphone beeps]

29:52.487 --> 29:53.622
Hello.

29:53.724 --> 29:56.558
I found this bag
up by Gate B17.

29:56.660 --> 29:58.321
Let me guess. Near the bathroom?

29:58.424 --> 30:01.123
-Yeah. How did you know?
-Happens all the time.

30:01.225 --> 30:03.162
It says "Sarah Grant" on it.

30:03.264 --> 30:05.528
-Okay. I'll take it from here.
-Okay. Good luck.

30:17.976 --> 30:19.315
[music fades out]

30:19.417 --> 30:20.576
[cellphone ringing]

30:24.783 --> 30:26.255
Hello?

30:26.357 --> 30:27.189
Credit or--

30:27.291 --> 30:28.254
Check.

30:29.359 --> 30:30.455
Go ahead.

30:30.858 --> 30:32.294
<i> "Where are you now?"</i>

30:32.396 --> 30:33.627
At the gate.

30:33.729 --> 30:35.393
Um, we're about to board.

30:36.569 --> 30:38.765
Um, what should I do? Go ahead.

30:38.867 --> 30:39.931
<i> "Do you have the packages?"</i>

30:40.033 --> 30:42.706
-Yes. Go ahead.
<i> -"Good."</i>

30:42.808 --> 30:45.204
[woman over PA]
<i> Passenger Sarah Grant,</i>

30:45.306 --> 30:47.976
<i> please come</i>
<i> to the lost-property counter.</i>

30:48.078 --> 30:52.448
<i> Passenger Sarah Grant.</i>
<i> Lost-property counter.</i>

30:52.550 --> 30:54.684
I'm gonna check it out.

30:54.786 --> 30:56.386
[operator]
<i> "Ignore everything else</i>

30:56.488 --> 30:58.251
<i> and await instructions."</i>

31:03.158 --> 31:05.091
[woman over PA]
<i> Passenger Sarah Grant,</i>

31:05.193 --> 31:07.623
please come
to the lost-property counter.

31:18.943 --> 31:21.378
<i> "Go to the post office</i>
<i> in concourse D</i>

31:21.480 --> 31:22.676
<i> and mail both packages.</i>

31:22.778 --> 31:24.915
<i> We will call you back."</i>

31:31.988 --> 31:34.819
Sir, may I help you
with something?

31:35.388 --> 31:36.922
[woman over PA]
<i> Passenger Sarah Grant,</i>

31:37.024 --> 31:39.655
<i> please report to Gate A29.</i>

31:39.757 --> 31:44.833
<i> Passenger Sarah Grant,</i>
<i> please report to Gate A29.</i>

31:44.935 --> 31:46.964
I'm never flying
your airline again.

31:47.066 --> 31:49.170
[dramatic music playing]

32:08.318 --> 32:10.960
-Where is she?
-No-show.

32:11.062 --> 32:13.491
They keep calling her name.
She didn't show up.

32:22.304 --> 32:24.134
Wanna do another lap?
If they're following her,

32:24.236 --> 32:25.468
they gotta be in here somewhere.

32:25.570 --> 32:27.302
[woman over PA]
<i> Final call for Grant,</i>

32:27.404 --> 32:30.310
<i> for Flight 8317 to Atlanta.</i>

32:31.946 --> 32:33.615
<i> Passenger Sarah Grant.</i>

32:33.717 --> 32:36.283
<i> Final call for Atlanta.</i>

32:36.915 --> 32:38.054
[sighs]

32:40.086 --> 32:41.618
They're not following her.

32:42.692 --> 32:43.994
What do you mean?

32:44.825 --> 32:45.891
We're made.

32:45.993 --> 32:48.196
[dramatic music continues]

32:50.060 --> 32:51.661
[sighs]

32:54.633 --> 32:56.639
-Where are you?
-[Rosetti]<i> You won't believe it,</i>

32:56.741 --> 32:58.371
but she's at the post office.

33:01.742 --> 33:02.774
Okay.

33:03.343 --> 33:09.115
And this one is
Norman, Oklahoma, 73019.

33:09.217 --> 33:11.649
Anything liquid,
fragile, hazardous?

33:11.751 --> 33:12.990
No.

33:15.961 --> 33:18.061
So, your tracking numbers
are right here.

33:18.163 --> 33:20.364
And if you wanna fill out
a survey, it's right there.

33:20.466 --> 33:21.762
-Okay.
-Okay?

33:21.864 --> 33:23.362
-Thanks.
-Thank you.

33:23.464 --> 33:29.666
So, the tracking number
is 840-59-70-0233803.

33:31.005 --> 33:32.669
[dramatic music continues]

33:50.529 --> 33:51.556
[music fades out]

33:55.030 --> 33:58.230
Okay. So, what can we learn?

33:58.332 --> 33:59.900
Hm? 'Cause
the airport security thing,

34:00.002 --> 34:01.871
it was smart, it was tight.

34:01.973 --> 34:03.502
Why send us
all the way to Pittsburgh?

34:03.604 --> 34:07.436
Since 2001, the TSA has closed
over 113 airport branches

34:07.538 --> 34:09.142
of the United States
Post Office.

34:09.244 --> 34:11.612
The only one remaining
inside security

34:11.714 --> 34:13.214
is Pittsburgh.

34:13.316 --> 34:16.345
All right. So, there's
two P.O. Box addresses.

34:16.447 --> 34:18.116
Split us up and keep us running.

34:18.218 --> 34:20.356
Looks like it's fucking working.

34:20.458 --> 34:21.620
Yep. Yep.

34:22.056 --> 34:23.357
You know what I think?

34:24.828 --> 34:26.560
I think I like this one.

34:26.929 --> 34:28.524
-Hoorah.
-[all chuckle]

34:28.626 --> 34:30.366
[Lee] They're smarter
than we thought.

34:30.469 --> 34:31.528
[chuckles]

34:31.631 --> 34:34.104
Hey, do you have those
tracking numbers for me?

34:36.207 --> 34:39.175
-There you go.
-Let's see where we're going.

34:42.679 --> 34:45.281
Check. Go ahead.

34:45.383 --> 34:48.314
"Good job. Please confirm that
you've sent all the documents

34:48.417 --> 34:50.252
-and have no further copies."
<i> -I confirm.</i>

34:50.354 --> 34:55.125
Were... Were they there today
at the airport? Go ahead.

34:56.054 --> 34:57.424
<i> "Yes."</i>

34:58.764 --> 35:01.697
So, you were, too? Go ahead.

35:01.799 --> 35:03.793
[keyboard keys clacking]

35:04.903 --> 35:06.595
<i> "Do not contact them yourself.</i>

35:06.697 --> 35:08.998
<i> Do not respond</i>
<i> if they contact you.</i>

35:09.100 --> 35:12.169
<i> They may try to scare you, and</i>
<i> they may try to make a deal.</i>

35:12.271 --> 35:14.244
But this is the only deal.

35:14.346 --> 35:17.413
<i> Once the packages arrive,</i>
<i> we will make them an offer.</i>

35:17.515 --> 35:21.112
<i> You're going to meet them once</i>
<i> to make the return yourself."</i>

35:21.214 --> 35:23.749
Do I have to? Go ahead.

35:24.652 --> 35:27.256
<i> "By then, you will have</i>
<i> all the leverage you need."</i>

35:28.585 --> 35:31.628
And you'll be there? Go ahead.

35:31.730 --> 35:33.657
[keyboard keys clacking]

35:33.759 --> 35:36.996
<i> "You will never meet us.</i>
<i> We are not bodyguards.</i>

35:37.098 --> 35:38.696
<i> We are intermediaries.</i>

35:38.798 --> 35:41.265
<i>We will broker a deal to return</i>
<i> the original documents</i>

35:41.367 --> 35:42.832
<i> and retain one safety copy</i>

35:42.934 --> 35:46.341
<i> to make sure Cybo Sementis</i>
<i> sticks to that deal.</i>

35:46.443 --> 35:49.141
<i> Follow our instructions,</i>
<i> and you will be protected.</i>

35:49.644 --> 35:52.209
<i> But if you don't,</i>
<i>you will put yourself in danger</i>

35:52.311 --> 35:53.650
<i> and we will walk away."</i>

35:53.752 --> 35:56.384
I understand. Go ahead.

35:59.189 --> 36:01.483
<i> "Your old phone</i>
<i> will be compromised.</i>

36:01.586 --> 36:03.723
<i> Put it in a pan of salt water.</i>

36:04.058 --> 36:05.459
<i> Use this one now."</i>

36:08.497 --> 36:09.991
<i> Your caller has hung up.</i>
<i> Thank you for using</i>

36:10.093 --> 36:12.668
<i> the Tri-State Relay Service.</i>
<i> Have a wonderful night.</i>

36:12.770 --> 36:13.698
[call disconnects]

36:27.480 --> 36:29.681
[ASG's "Survive Sunrise"
playing]

36:56.012 --> 36:58.143
<i> ♪ Strike for your eyes ♪</i>

36:58.245 --> 37:01.251
<i> ♪ When I'm seeking ♪</i>

37:03.019 --> 37:04.952
<i> ♪ A heart in the sky ♪</i>

37:05.054 --> 37:08.790
<i> ♪ Worth believing ♪</i>

37:08.892 --> 37:11.987
<i> ♪ When I feel ♪</i>

37:13.558 --> 37:16.198
<i> ♪ Like suffering some... ♪</i>

37:16.300 --> 37:18.232
-[line ringing]
-[music volume turns down]

37:18.334 --> 37:21.364
Hey. Yeah.
I got a camera in position.

37:21.466 --> 37:23.206
<i> But I don't got nothing.</i>

37:23.308 --> 37:25.771
<i> What about you?</i>
<i> How's Michigan treating you?</i>

37:25.873 --> 37:28.070
[Rosetti]<i> I'm guessing better</i>
<i> than Bumfuck, Oklahoma.</i>

37:28.172 --> 37:31.211
-[Ryan chuckles]<i> Damn.</i>
-[Rosetti]<i> It's really pretty.</i>

37:31.313 --> 37:38.519
<i> ♪ Like those suffering some ♪</i>

37:40.224 --> 37:42.520
-Hi.
-Hi. I wanna pick up a package

37:42.622 --> 37:44.822
for my friend Archie.
He's got box 521.

37:44.924 --> 37:47.526
I have the tracking number,
but I forgot the key.

37:47.628 --> 37:50.327
Would you be able
just to grab it for me?

37:50.429 --> 37:51.461
Well, I'm afraid, ma'am,

37:51.564 --> 37:53.101
that regulations
do not permit me

37:53.203 --> 37:55.035
to open mailboxes
for our clients.

37:55.137 --> 37:57.005
-Oh, no. Really?
-Sorry.

37:57.375 --> 38:00.171
It's my fault. Should've
remembered the darn key.

38:00.273 --> 38:01.372
-Yeah.
-[sighs]

38:01.474 --> 38:05.376
Just... My dog is really sick.

38:05.479 --> 38:08.883
-Oh.
-Yeah. My head is a mess.

38:08.985 --> 38:11.285
I... I'm sorry.

38:11.387 --> 38:13.450
-Well, that's a shame, ma'am.
-Yeah.

38:13.553 --> 38:16.356
She's just a... tired old girl.

38:16.458 --> 38:19.791
-Aw.
-Won't be too much longer now.

38:20.359 --> 38:21.593
[Rosetti sighs]

38:21.696 --> 38:23.594
I don't suppose
you'd be able to just check

38:23.696 --> 38:25.797
to see if the package
has arrived?

38:26.396 --> 38:27.964
Oh. Um...

38:28.970 --> 38:30.104
Uh, okay.

38:30.207 --> 38:31.770
-Thank you.
-You wait here.

38:36.340 --> 38:37.644
[sighs]

38:40.878 --> 38:42.981
I'm sorry, ma'am.
There's nothing there.

38:43.083 --> 38:47.183
Well, it was sent Priority Mail.
It should have already arrived.

38:47.286 --> 38:48.688
I'm sorry.

38:49.761 --> 38:51.757
Huh. Okay.

38:52.457 --> 38:54.059
Not a good day.

38:54.762 --> 38:57.896
Did your friend recently move,
by any chance?

38:57.998 --> 39:01.233
If they did, there would be
a forwarding address on file,

39:01.335 --> 39:03.336
and if it was rerouted,

39:03.438 --> 39:05.369
well, that could explain
the delay.

39:05.471 --> 39:07.308
Yes. Mail forwarding.

39:07.410 --> 39:09.006
Oh, my gosh.
That makes total sense.

39:09.108 --> 39:13.142
He just moved here, actually.
Can you tell me something?

39:13.244 --> 39:17.612
Will the new destination show up
on that old tracking number?

39:17.714 --> 39:18.987
Now, there's the thing.

39:19.089 --> 39:20.120
Tracking does not always

39:20.222 --> 39:21.553
carry over to forwarding

39:21.655 --> 39:24.527
because they're
different services.

39:24.629 --> 39:25.623
Huh.

39:25.725 --> 39:27.925
[Bush Tetras' "Too Many Creeps"
playing]

39:29.298 --> 39:32.329
<i> ♪ I just don't wanna go ♪</i>

39:32.665 --> 39:35.768
<i> ♪ Out in the streets no more ♪</i>

39:36.503 --> 39:39.269
<i> ♪ I just don't wanna go ♪</i>

39:39.705 --> 39:42.670
<i> ♪ Out in the streets no more ♪</i>

39:43.140 --> 39:46.345
<i> ♪ Because these people</i>
<i> They give me ♪</i>

39:46.448 --> 39:48.147
<i> ♪ They give me the creeps ♪</i>

39:48.249 --> 39:49.919
<i> ♪ Anymore ♪</i>

39:50.021 --> 39:51.316
<i> ♪ Too many creeps ♪</i>

39:51.418 --> 39:53.120
<i> ♪ Too many creeps ♪</i>

39:53.222 --> 39:54.583
<i> ♪ Too many creeps ♪</i>

39:54.685 --> 39:55.584
<i> ♪ Too many creeps ♪</i>

39:55.686 --> 39:56.893
<i> ♪ I don't wanna ♪</i>

39:56.995 --> 39:58.158
<i> ♪ It's the worst ♪</i>

39:58.260 --> 39:59.390
<i> ♪ It's the worst ♪</i>

39:59.492 --> 40:01.194
<i> ♪ It's the worst ♪</i>

40:01.296 --> 40:02.996
<i> ♪ It's the worst ♪</i>

40:03.098 --> 40:04.027
<i> ♪ Yeah! ♪</i>

40:22.213 --> 40:24.949
[operator]<i> "This is a message</i>
<i> for Mr. Franklin.</i>

40:25.051 --> 40:27.951
We've been given a copy
of a food safety assessment

40:28.053 --> 40:31.591
of Cybo Sementis's
Fertile Crescent wheat program

40:31.694 --> 40:34.360
by Sarah Grant,
a former employee of yours,

40:34.463 --> 40:36.466
<i> who has engaged our services.</i>

40:36.568 --> 40:40.897
<i> It is 311 pages long</i>
<i> and contains two appendices.</i>

40:41.000 --> 40:43.202
In exchange for
your unconditional agreement

40:43.304 --> 40:44.704
to leave her alone,

40:44.806 --> 40:46.539
our client would like
to return this document

40:46.641 --> 40:48.808
and agree
never to mention it again."

41:06.031 --> 41:07.992
[dramatic music playing]

41:44.065 --> 41:45.962
[operator]<i> "Our client would</i>
<i> like to return this document</i>

41:46.064 --> 41:47.966
<i> and agree</i>
<i> never to mention it again.</i>

41:48.068 --> 41:51.471
<i> All communication with her</i>
<i> must come through us.</i>

41:51.573 --> 41:55.171
<i> Leave a message</i>
<i> on 646-167-1573.</i>

41:55.273 --> 41:57.977
<i> We will contact you</i>
<i> with further instructions."</i>

41:58.079 --> 42:00.479
Callback number is the same.
Goes to the messaging service.

42:00.581 --> 42:03.013
Check out the answer service HQ.

42:03.115 --> 42:05.483
I tried that. Client protection
is super tight.

42:05.585 --> 42:08.118
[cellphone ringing nearby]

42:11.922 --> 42:13.860
[cellphone continues ringing]

42:17.301 --> 42:20.064
[cellphone continues ringing]

42:23.835 --> 42:27.674
[cellphone continues ringing]

42:27.776 --> 42:29.476
-Hello?
-[operator]<i> A person is calling</i>

42:29.578 --> 42:31.007
<i> from the</i>
<i> Tri-State Relay Service.</i>

42:31.109 --> 42:33.209
<i> Have you received</i>
<i> a relay call before?</i>

42:35.180 --> 42:38.313
<i> "You've been harassing</i>
<i> our client, Sarah Grant.</i>

42:39.057 --> 42:40.188
<i> Please stop."</i>

42:40.290 --> 42:41.523
She violated her NDA,

42:41.625 --> 42:43.158
and she's holding on
to stolen research,

42:43.260 --> 42:45.458
so no can do. Go ahead.

42:45.561 --> 42:48.125
<i> "And now she's given it to us.</i>

42:48.227 --> 42:51.400
In case you're doubting this,
page nine starts with:

42:51.502 --> 42:54.667
'The enhancement
of clerodane diterpenes

42:54.769 --> 42:56.404
in Fertile Crescent
sample 7...'"

42:56.506 --> 42:58.674
All right. I understand.
Go ahead.

43:00.504 --> 43:04.513
<i> "We've left word at the office</i>
<i> of Cybo Sementis's CEO,</i>

43:04.615 --> 43:06.914
<i> Mr. Franklin.</i>
<i> We await his response."</i>

43:07.016 --> 43:09.179
Mr. Franklin passed on your
message. [whispering] Track it.

43:09.281 --> 43:12.721
And he's authorized us to speak
on his behalf. Go ahead.

43:12.823 --> 43:16.121
"Who am I speaking to,
and what is your position?"

43:16.223 --> 43:19.662
Well, my name is Steve Dawson.
Don't look it up. It's not real.

43:19.764 --> 43:22.128
And my team is tasked
with returning the documents.

43:22.230 --> 43:23.463
Go ahead.

43:23.866 --> 43:26.600
<i> "We wish to return them</i>
<i> as soon as possible,</i>

43:26.702 --> 43:28.097
<i> but in order</i>
<i> to protect our client,</i>

43:28.200 --> 43:30.099
<i> we are ready</i>
<i> to send them simultaneously</i>

43:30.201 --> 43:32.837
to all appropriate
law-enforcement agencies

43:32.939 --> 43:35.244
as well as every major
media outlet

43:35.346 --> 43:36.676
<i>if you don't fully cooperate...</i>

43:36.778 --> 43:38.976
-[mouthing]
<i> -...with our requests."</i>

43:39.078 --> 43:40.916
We'll do our best to cooperate.
Go ahead.

43:41.018 --> 43:43.779
"There will be no more threats
to our client, no surveillance,

43:43.881 --> 43:45.446
<i> including phone taps.</i>

43:45.548 --> 43:48.455
<i> Once we are satisfied</i>
<i> with our client's security,</i>

43:48.557 --> 43:49.822
<i> we'll return the original.</i>

43:49.925 --> 43:52.591
We will keep a single
secure copy as insurance

43:52.693 --> 43:53.922
for our client's protection."

43:54.024 --> 43:55.264
How do we know to trust you?

43:55.366 --> 43:57.695
You could be anyone. Go ahead.

43:57.798 --> 43:59.600
<i> "You will be our client, too.</i>

43:59.702 --> 44:01.899
<i> You will be required</i>
<i> to pay a fee.</i>

44:02.001 --> 44:03.902
<i> We work for both parties</i>
<i> to ensure</i>

44:04.005 --> 44:05.774
<i> that the job is done</i>
<i> with no loose ends.</i>

44:05.876 --> 44:09.039
<i> It is in all our interests</i>
<i> for it to run smoothly."</i>

44:09.141 --> 44:11.144
That's very kind of you.
How much is the fee?

44:11.246 --> 44:12.473
Go ahead.

44:12.575 --> 44:15.113
<i>-"Half a million dollars cash."</i>
-That's a lot of money.

44:15.215 --> 44:17.312
How do we trust your client's
intentions? Go ahead.

44:17.414 --> 44:19.414
<i> "You were tapping</i>
<i> our client's first calls.</i>

44:19.516 --> 44:22.417
<i> You know as much about</i>
<i> their intentions as we do."</i>

44:24.256 --> 44:26.594
I'm gonna have to run it
internally. Go ahead.

44:26.696 --> 44:28.022
<i> "You have until</i>
<i> end of day tomorrow</i>

44:28.124 --> 44:29.595
<i> to confirm your acceptance."</i>

44:29.697 --> 44:31.366
Yeah, understood. Go ahead.

44:31.468 --> 44:32.697
<i> "Now get a new parking spot</i>

44:32.799 --> 44:34.902
<i>and stay away from our client."</i>

44:36.037 --> 44:37.870
<i> Your caller has hung up.</i>
<i> Thank you for using</i>

44:37.973 --> 44:39.735
<i> Tri-State Relay Service.</i>
<i> Have a wonderful--</i>

44:39.837 --> 44:40.738
[disconnect tone]

44:40.840 --> 44:43.042
[suspenseful music playing]

45:11.603 --> 45:12.603
Let's go.

45:12.705 --> 45:13.776
[engine starts]

45:34.198 --> 45:35.329
Credit or debit?

45:35.431 --> 45:36.562
[Sarah]<i> Check.</i>

45:36.965 --> 45:40.695
The surveillance van is gone.
Thank you.

45:40.797 --> 45:43.036
[beeping]

45:46.237 --> 45:49.173
<i> "Good. Now we wait</i>
<i> for a few days.</i>

45:49.275 --> 45:51.372
<i> You will need to be patient</i>
<i> and stay calm.</i>

45:51.475 --> 45:53.077
<i> Once they fulfill</i>
<i> their end of the deal,</i>

45:53.179 --> 45:54.550
<i> we'll arrange</i>
<i> to return the documents</i>

45:54.652 --> 45:56.918
<i> before the SEC deadline</i>
<i> next week.</i>

45:57.020 --> 45:59.349
<i> After that, you will need</i>
<i> to relocate for a while.</i>

45:59.451 --> 46:01.416
<i> Ideally, somewhere</i>
<i> in this country you can reach</i>

46:01.518 --> 46:03.926
<i> by public transportation</i>
<i> so they can't track you.</i>

46:04.028 --> 46:07.228
<i> It is for your protection</i>
<i> and shouldn't be permanent."</i>

46:07.330 --> 46:08.897
I understand.

46:10.101 --> 46:11.196
Go ahead.

46:12.703 --> 46:15.530
Hey, um, the weather
is getting better.

46:15.632 --> 46:21.140
Um, is it okay if I spend
some time outside? Go ahead.

46:23.042 --> 46:24.979
<i> "They should leave you alone.</i>

46:25.081 --> 46:27.950
<i> If you see anything</i>
<i>that worries you, let us know."</i>

46:28.052 --> 46:28.978
How?

46:29.447 --> 46:33.086
You're not that easy
to get ahold of. Go ahead.

46:35.386 --> 46:37.392
<i> "After 6 p.m. each day,</i>
<i> leave a message</i>

46:37.494 --> 46:38.993
<i> at the number you have.</i>

46:39.825 --> 46:41.660
<i> Just one word.</i>

46:42.096 --> 46:44.931
<i> If something is wrong,</i>
<i> say, 'Weather.'</i>

46:45.033 --> 46:48.365
<i> If everything's okay,</i>
<i> say, 'Alright.'"</i>

46:50.775 --> 46:53.935
"All right" is two words,
not one. Go ahead.

46:54.037 --> 46:55.845
[teletype beeping]

46:57.415 --> 46:58.875
[keyboard keys clacking]

46:58.977 --> 47:01.015
"Ever listen to The Who?

47:02.051 --> 47:04.952
<i> First album.</i>
<i> First track on the B side."</i>

47:05.054 --> 47:07.752
-[keyboard keys clacking]
-[teletype disconnecting]

47:08.188 --> 47:10.259
<i> Your caller has hung up.</i>
<i> Thank you for--</i>

47:10.361 --> 47:11.289
[disconnect tone]

47:13.498 --> 47:15.997
[siren wailing in distance]

47:23.304 --> 47:27.074
I see you at meetings,
but I've never seen you share.

47:29.842 --> 47:31.177
How long you sober?

47:31.843 --> 47:33.311
Nineteen months.

47:34.077 --> 47:35.778
What step you on?

47:36.247 --> 47:38.349
I've been kicking around
step four.

47:39.118 --> 47:40.818
-Mm-hmm.
-For a minute, actually.

47:40.920 --> 47:42.884
-Moral inventory?
-Yeah.

47:42.986 --> 47:44.086
Resentments?

47:44.188 --> 47:46.659
Yeah. I got a lot of those.

47:46.761 --> 47:48.623
[chuckles] You working?

47:49.829 --> 47:50.966
What kind of gig?

47:52.336 --> 47:53.931
Mostly delivery.

47:54.034 --> 47:56.364
Parcels, food, stuff like that.

47:56.466 --> 47:58.470
I got a little something
on the side, too.

47:58.572 --> 47:59.502
Legal?

48:00.476 --> 48:01.603
[chuckles]

48:03.008 --> 48:04.606
You don't wanna tell me?

48:06.581 --> 48:07.950
Dangerous?

48:10.718 --> 48:12.383
We're addicts, Jon.

48:14.019 --> 48:15.418
We do addicty things.

48:15.520 --> 48:18.455
And we just gotta be
aware of them and pull back

48:18.557 --> 48:21.422
so we don't replace
one addiction with a new one.

48:21.524 --> 48:23.124
What if what you're doing
is important

48:23.226 --> 48:24.964
and somebody has to do it?

48:25.066 --> 48:27.937
Well, you have to decide
how important.

48:30.168 --> 48:32.170
Listen, however you're managing,

48:32.272 --> 48:35.406
you just don't need to do it
all on your own.

48:36.578 --> 48:38.112
The fact is...

48:38.976 --> 48:40.081
you can't.

48:47.654 --> 48:49.519
[beeping]

48:53.792 --> 48:56.493
[beeping]

48:59.362 --> 49:01.466
They've agreed to your terms.

49:02.002 --> 49:04.039
How do we transfer the money?

49:05.677 --> 49:07.405
What do you want us to do next?

49:09.077 --> 49:12.377
"Send unmarked cash
to P.O. Box 897,

49:12.479 --> 49:16.717
<i> Landers, California, 92285,</i>
<i> overnight priority.</i>

49:16.820 --> 49:18.050
When it has been
safely received,

49:18.152 --> 49:20.416
we will issue
further instructions.

49:20.519 --> 49:24.322
<i> Any delay</i>
<i> and the document goes public."</i>

49:24.424 --> 49:26.392
<i> Your caller has hung up.</i>
<i> Thank you for using</i>

49:26.494 --> 49:29.427
<i> the Tri-State Relay Service.</i>
<i> And have a wonderful day.</i>

49:30.060 --> 49:31.561
He's brazen.

49:34.635 --> 49:36.434
Okay. Oh.

49:36.536 --> 49:38.499
[Ryan] How long do the batteries
in those things last?

49:38.601 --> 49:41.172
[Lee] Four or five days.
Should be enough.

49:41.274 --> 49:42.979
-[Ryan] Right?
-[Dawson] Fuck you, pal.

49:45.213 --> 49:48.446
-Box it up.
-Glad I don't have to pay it.

49:50.150 --> 49:51.716
[Lee] The tracker is activated.

49:51.818 --> 49:53.487
That's cool.

49:54.190 --> 49:56.355
[The Heliocentrics'
"Made Of The Sun" playing]

50:04.164 --> 50:08.636
<i> ♪ Every piece of the puzzle ♪</i>

50:08.738 --> 50:12.300
<i> ♪ Falls into one ♪</i>

50:12.402 --> 50:16.343
<i> ♪ I'm made of the flesh ♪</i>

50:16.812 --> 50:20.843
<i> ♪ I'm made of the sun ♪</i>

50:21.412 --> 50:26.181
<i> ♪ Sketchbook falls wide open ♪</i>

50:26.283 --> 50:29.918
<i> ♪ Just be like a child ♪</i>

50:30.454 --> 50:33.756
<i> ♪ How can we be different ♪</i>

50:34.192 --> 50:37.692
<i> ♪ Born to be wild ♪</i>

50:37.794 --> 50:45.166
<i> ♪ My seed of insight</i>
<i> Seems so slow to grow ♪</i>

50:45.735 --> 50:51.777
<i> ♪ Coming to fruit now</i>
<i> Aware, I know ♪</i>

50:51.879 --> 50:53.676
<i> ♪ I felt your ♪</i>

50:53.778 --> 51:00.221
<i> ♪ I felt your presence</i>
<i> Right from the start ♪</i>

51:01.054 --> 51:03.691
<i> ♪ No more as strangers ♪</i>

51:03.793 --> 51:08.229
<i> ♪ Will we ever part ♪</i>

51:09.196 --> 51:14.196
<i> ♪ Oh, and last of the hope ♪</i>

51:14.298 --> 51:18.134
<i> ♪ Born from despair ♪</i>

51:18.236 --> 51:20.334
<i> ♪ End of the road ♪</i>

51:20.436 --> 51:24.512
<i> ♪ But I pray, I pray ♪</i>

51:24.614 --> 51:26.808
<i> ♪ I pray ♪</i>

51:27.852 --> 51:31.752
<i> ♪ Teary-eyed on the floor ♪</i>

51:31.854 --> 51:35.724
<i> ♪ I found inspiration ♪</i>

51:35.826 --> 51:38.660
<i> ♪ What hurt me the most ♪</i>

51:38.762 --> 51:42.459
<i> ♪ Brought incarnation ♪</i>

51:42.562 --> 51:44.326
[automated voice]
<i> Special answering service.</i>

51:44.428 --> 51:47.837
<i> Inbox 482. One new message.</i>

51:47.939 --> 51:49.199
[Dawson]
<i> The package has been sent.</i>

51:49.301 --> 51:53.339
<i> Tracking number 4739-27721.</i>

51:53.441 --> 51:55.039
<i> The filing deadline's less</i>
<i> than a week away,</i>

51:55.141 --> 51:56.871
<i> so ball's in your court.</i>

51:59.279 --> 52:01.117
[Hoffman on message]<i> All right.</i>

52:02.345 --> 52:04.252
[voice mail beeps]

52:07.255 --> 52:09.721
[Sarah on message]
<i> All... right.</i>

52:09.824 --> 52:11.089
[chuckles]

52:11.192 --> 52:13.426
[Dabrye's "Fightscene" playing]

52:27.777 --> 52:30.040
<i> ♪ Fight scene ♪</i>

52:30.142 --> 52:32.181
<i> ♪ Fight scene ♪</i>

52:37.915 --> 52:40.382
<i> ♪ Ride on 'em, buckle up</i>
<i> Hands up, knuckle up ♪</i>

52:40.485 --> 52:42.450
<i> ♪ Fight scene, fight scene ♪</i>

52:43.019 --> 52:45.354
<i> ♪ Ride on 'em, buckle up</i>
<i> Hands up, knuckle up ♪</i>

52:45.457 --> 52:47.427
<i> ♪ Fight scene, fight scene ♪</i>

52:48.294 --> 52:50.199
[communicating in sign language]

52:50.865 --> 52:51.728
[song stops]

52:57.668 --> 52:59.637
You know what it is, man.
Work, work.

53:02.813 --> 53:05.775
Yeah. Uh, I need an ID.

53:14.584 --> 53:17.589
Minnesota? Yeah. That's fine.

53:22.095 --> 53:23.463
Getting harder, huh?

53:25.969 --> 53:27.467
Three days? That's cool, man.

53:29.139 --> 53:31.768
Oh, price--
Oh, motherfucker. Okay.

53:32.972 --> 53:34.039
What?

53:34.608 --> 53:38.313
Bro, come on, man.
You always bullshitting me, bro.

53:39.309 --> 53:40.810
Yo, you know me.

53:41.817 --> 53:42.944
What is it?

53:43.884 --> 53:45.048
Or what?

53:45.150 --> 53:46.585
You want four?

53:49.654 --> 53:51.887
[Agnes Obel's
"Close Watch" playing]

53:54.625 --> 53:59.668
<i> ♪ Never win and never lose ♪</i>

54:00.204 --> 54:04.037
<i> ♪ There's nothing left</i>
<i> To choose ♪</i>

54:04.140 --> 54:08.343
<i> ♪ Between right and wrong ♪</i>

54:11.380 --> 54:15.810
<i> ♪ Nothing lost</i>
<i> And nothing gained ♪</i>

54:15.913 --> 54:19.981
<i> ♪ Still things</i>
<i> Ain't quite the same ♪</i>

54:20.891 --> 54:24.392
<i> ♪ Between you and me ♪</i>

54:27.662 --> 54:34.303
<i> ♪ I keep a close watch</i>
<i> On this heart of mine ♪</i>

54:36.172 --> 54:38.706
<i> ♪ I keep a close watch on-- ♪</i>

54:38.808 --> 54:39.874
[song stops]

54:39.976 --> 54:40.940
[automated voice]<i> ...482.</i>

54:41.042 --> 54:41.776
<i> One new message.</i>

54:41.878 --> 54:42.977
[voice mail beeps]

54:43.079 --> 54:44.773
[on message]<i> This is Hoffman.</i>

54:45.075 --> 54:49.682
<i> Optimo Pharmaceutical's</i>
<i>history of fraud is incredible.</i>

54:49.784 --> 54:53.184
<i> They just pay the fines</i>
<i> and keep doing the same thing.</i>

54:53.853 --> 54:56.952
<i> How many people have died</i>
<i> because of their lies?</i>

54:57.962 --> 54:59.955
<i> Lies that I was a part of.</i>

55:02.098 --> 55:04.025
<i> I missed my niece's baptism.</i>

55:06.762 --> 55:08.931
<i>I wonder what else I'm missing.</i>

55:12.876 --> 55:14.641
[voice mail beeps]

55:15.244 --> 55:17.412
[Sarah on message]<i> All... right.</i>

55:20.380 --> 55:22.549
<i> All is right with the world.</i>

55:24.218 --> 55:25.684
<i> Joke, right?</i> [chuckles]

55:30.160 --> 55:32.691
<i> I wonder</i>
<i> what your life is like.</i>

55:42.538 --> 55:46.705
[scoffs]<i> I wonder</i>
<i>if you even listen this far in.</i>

55:48.878 --> 55:50.874
[liquid pouring]

55:52.850 --> 55:54.680
<i> Are you lonely?</i>

55:55.346 --> 55:56.878
[Sarah sips]

55:56.980 --> 55:58.615
-[clicking]
<i> -♪ I'm in the phone booth</i>

55:58.717 --> 56:00.686
<i> ♪ It's the one</i>
<i> Across the hall ♪</i>

56:00.788 --> 56:03.920
<i> ♪ If you don't answer</i>
<i> I'll ring it off the wall ♪</i>

56:04.022 --> 56:07.758
<i> ♪ I know she's there</i>
<i> But I just had to call ♪</i>

56:07.860 --> 56:14.402
<i> ♪ Don't leave me hanging</i>
<i> On the telephone ♪</i>

56:14.504 --> 56:21.502
<i> ♪ Don't leave me hanging</i>
<i> On the telephone ♪</i>

56:21.604 --> 56:23.445
[voice mail beeps]

56:26.212 --> 56:27.548
[train rumbling]

56:34.024 --> 56:36.755
[keyboard keys clacking]

57:04.285 --> 57:06.488
[poignant music playing]

57:23.771 --> 57:27.909
[automated voice]
<i> Inbox 482. No new messages.</i>

57:28.011 --> 57:29.643
[voice mail beeps]

57:37.846 --> 57:40.049
[poignant music continues]

58:03.112 --> 58:05.107
[engine starts]

58:11.186 --> 58:13.951
[cellphone ringing]

58:18.025 --> 58:19.020
Yes.

58:19.122 --> 58:20.824
[Jon]<i> This is</i>
<i> Tri-State Relay Service.</i>

58:20.926 --> 58:22.490
<i> Have you received</i>
<i> a relay call before?</i>

58:22.592 --> 58:24.061
Yes. Check.

58:24.497 --> 58:26.794
<i> Sorry I didn't call.</i>

58:26.896 --> 58:29.234
Is something wrong? Go ahead.

58:29.836 --> 58:31.936
<i> I just wanted to see</i>
<i> if you were okay.</i>

58:33.541 --> 58:36.106
Yeah. I'm fine. What about you?

58:36.542 --> 58:38.844
Are you okay? Go ahead.

58:40.615 --> 58:43.712
I'm fine.
I listened to your message.

58:43.814 --> 58:45.616
Interesting musical choice.

58:45.718 --> 58:48.417
<i> Oh, God.</i>
<i> You listened to the end.</i>

58:48.519 --> 58:51.356
Sorry. Go ahead.

58:52.026 --> 58:55.190
<i> How did you know there was</i>
<i> an original to that song?</i>

58:56.130 --> 58:57.692
Google.

58:57.794 --> 59:00.328
I use modern technology.

59:00.764 --> 59:02.533
Feels like you don't.

59:03.235 --> 59:08.836
So, what else do you listen to
aside from The Who? Go ahead.

59:09.305 --> 59:12.276
-Who said I listened to them?
<i> -Oh, come on.</i>

59:12.612 --> 59:14.275
<i> I've got time on my hands.</i>

59:14.377 --> 59:17.381
<i> I can listen to anything</i>
<i> you can recommend. Go ahead.</i>

59:18.150 --> 59:22.086
<i> I recommend we keep</i>
<i> communication to a minimum.</i>

59:22.188 --> 59:28.160
Well, you stuck around to listen
to all of my last message.

59:28.262 --> 59:30.599
So, are you?

59:31.265 --> 59:32.733
<i> Go ahead.</i>

59:34.532 --> 59:36.068
Am I what?

59:36.170 --> 59:37.639
Lonely.

59:38.502 --> 59:39.905
Go ahead.

59:43.407 --> 59:46.513
<i>It's strange talking to someone</i>
<i> who knows so much about you</i>

59:46.615 --> 59:48.815
<i> when you know so little</i>
<i> about them.</i>

59:50.012 --> 59:52.214
<i> May I ask you a question?</i>

59:52.681 --> 59:54.183
Go ahead.

59:56.457 --> 59:58.319
<i> It depends what it is.</i>

01:00:01.561 --> 01:00:03.665
Has it ever gone wrong?

01:00:05.431 --> 01:00:07.267
<i> Go ahead.</i>

01:00:07.369 --> 01:00:09.132
Sometimes people run.

01:00:10.902 --> 01:00:14.368
Sometimes we have to walk away.

01:00:16.073 --> 01:00:19.879
The instructions,
not everybody listens.

01:00:22.386 --> 01:00:25.049
I'll try hard to behave myself.

01:00:26.056 --> 01:00:27.623
<i> Good night.</i>

01:00:28.587 --> 01:00:29.757
[disconnect tone]

01:00:38.401 --> 01:00:40.834
That was a new number. Run it.

01:00:49.642 --> 01:00:51.713
Nice. It's already off.

01:01:03.924 --> 01:01:06.522
-[clerk] Okay, you're all set.
-Thank you.

01:01:06.624 --> 01:01:07.590
-Hi.
-Hi.

01:01:07.959 --> 01:01:09.693
I have a mailbox in California.

01:01:09.795 --> 01:01:10.991
That's where I normally live.

01:01:11.093 --> 01:01:12.599
But I'm going away to Europe

01:01:12.701 --> 01:01:14.869
for a month on business.
I know. Poor me.

01:01:14.971 --> 01:01:18.300
Um, could I please have all
my mail forwarded to my cousin

01:01:18.402 --> 01:01:20.938
-who lives in Poughkeepsie?
-Yes. That's possible.

01:01:21.040 --> 01:01:23.909
And she's actually moving.
So, what do I do?

01:01:24.011 --> 01:01:26.206
-Send it to General Delivery?
-Yep. You got it.

01:01:26.308 --> 01:01:27.878
She'll need an ID
to pick anything up.

01:01:27.980 --> 01:01:30.645
All right. Cool.
Let's do that. Thank you.

01:01:31.315 --> 01:01:33.819
So, it'll be coming
from Landers, California.

01:01:33.921 --> 01:01:35.586
And the name of the person
it's going to?

01:01:35.688 --> 01:01:39.928
Sarah with an "H." Grant.

01:01:40.030 --> 01:01:41.092
Mm-hmm.

01:01:42.826 --> 01:01:45.063
[indistinct chatter]

01:01:45.862 --> 01:01:48.066
[traffic humming]

01:01:48.734 --> 01:01:50.970
[siren wailing nearby]

01:01:53.910 --> 01:01:56.140
-[voice mail beeps]
-[on message]<i> This is Dawson.</i>

01:01:56.242 --> 01:01:58.546
<i> According to the USPS,</i>
<i> the money's been delivered.</i>

01:01:58.648 --> 01:02:00.373
<i> The SEC filing</i>
<i> is in three days,</i>

01:02:00.476 --> 01:02:02.349
<i> so we're expecting</i>
<i> handover arrangements</i>

01:02:02.451 --> 01:02:03.614
<i> as soon as possible.</i>

01:02:03.716 --> 01:02:05.248
<i> But we have a problem.</i>

01:02:05.350 --> 01:02:08.721
<i> You told Mr. Franklin</i>
<i> you had a 311-page document.</i>

01:02:08.823 --> 01:02:11.492
<i> But the full report</i>
<i> is 327 pages</i>

01:02:11.594 --> 01:02:13.922
<i> with a 16-page</i>
<i> third appendix.</i>

01:02:14.024 --> 01:02:15.830
<i>We need all the pages returned.</i>

01:02:15.932 --> 01:02:17.760
<i> Otherwise, why did we pay</i>
<i> half a million dollars?</i>

01:02:17.862 --> 01:02:18.967
<i> Tick-tock, motherfucker.</i>

01:02:19.069 --> 01:02:20.098
[beeping]

01:02:23.465 --> 01:02:25.373
[operator]
<i> "You told us that you had sent</i>

01:02:25.475 --> 01:02:27.303
<i> all the relevant documents."</i>

01:02:28.408 --> 01:02:29.577
I did.

01:02:29.679 --> 01:02:31.806
<i> -Go ahead.</i>
<i> -"What about Appendix C?</i>

01:02:31.908 --> 01:02:33.545
<i> It's missing."</i>

01:02:34.115 --> 01:02:36.278
There was no info there.
It was all just small print.

01:02:36.380 --> 01:02:40.222
<i> Nothing pertaining</i>
<i> to the research. Go ahead.</i>

01:02:40.324 --> 01:02:42.951
[dramatic music playing]

01:02:43.053 --> 01:02:44.489
"Why would you leave it out?"

01:02:44.591 --> 01:02:46.124
I just didn't think.

01:02:47.595 --> 01:02:49.091
<i> "Do you still have it?"</i>

01:02:49.193 --> 01:02:51.391
-Yes, I do. Go ahead.
<i> -"They need it."</i>

01:02:51.494 --> 01:02:54.601
I will send it to you
like before. Go ahead.

01:02:54.703 --> 01:02:57.301
<i> "Takes too long.</i>
<i> You were warned.</i>

01:02:57.403 --> 01:03:00.534
<i> You must follow the steps,</i>
<i> or we can't protect you."</i>

01:03:03.342 --> 01:03:07.816
Please don't leave me to do this
by myself. [cries softly]

01:03:16.491 --> 01:03:18.453
[train horn blaring]

01:03:31.375 --> 01:03:34.106
[tense music playing]

01:03:46.089 --> 01:03:49.891
"There's a newsstand on the
corner of 7th and West 46th.

01:03:49.993 --> 01:03:52.192
<i> Put the envelope in the pages</i>
<i> of the bottom copy</i>

01:03:52.294 --> 01:03:55.594
<i> of</i> The Washington Post,<i> which</i>
<i>is the second pile on the left.</i>

01:03:55.696 --> 01:03:56.859
<i> Then leave the area."</i>

01:03:56.961 --> 01:03:59.164
[tense music continues]

01:04:17.080 --> 01:04:19.283
[siren wailing nearby]

01:04:27.427 --> 01:04:28.396
Go.

01:04:28.498 --> 01:04:30.459
[tense music continues]

01:04:42.443 --> 01:04:43.978
[buzzes]

01:04:51.653 --> 01:04:53.647
[tense music continues]

01:05:00.192 --> 01:05:01.960
-Thank you.
-[clerk] Yeah. No problem.

01:05:02.062 --> 01:05:03.627
-How's it going?
-[clerk] It's going.

01:05:03.729 --> 01:05:04.893
[Jon] Yeah?

01:05:04.995 --> 01:05:06.363
[clerk] Just that?

01:05:13.002 --> 01:05:14.107
[whistles]

01:05:17.272 --> 01:05:19.442
[tense music continues]

01:05:26.652 --> 01:05:29.154
[Ryan] Could I get your photo?
Doing this thing on New Yorkers

01:05:29.256 --> 01:05:32.119
in their natural habitat.
You know what I'm saying?

01:05:32.221 --> 01:05:33.929
[tense music continues]

01:05:35.958 --> 01:05:37.361
Come on!

01:05:49.279 --> 01:05:52.045
I left it in the<i> Post,</i> bottom
copy, left pile like you said.

01:05:52.147 --> 01:05:55.450
"The<i> Washington Post</i>
is second from the left."

01:05:55.552 --> 01:05:57.480
Second from the left.

01:05:59.048 --> 01:06:00.753
I'm so sorry.

01:06:01.355 --> 01:06:05.119
Everything happened so fast.
Um, I'll come back for it.

01:06:05.221 --> 01:06:07.261
[keyboard keys clacking]

01:06:07.363 --> 01:06:10.595
<i>"It'll be gone by then. Did you</i>
<i> know you were being followed?"</i>

01:06:11.164 --> 01:06:12.963
[Sarah]
No. I thought they stopped that.

01:06:13.065 --> 01:06:14.970
I'm so sorry. It's my fault.

01:06:15.570 --> 01:06:17.131
Don't walk away.

01:06:17.233 --> 01:06:19.000
[keyboard keys clacking]

01:06:19.102 --> 01:06:21.603
[disconnect tone]

01:06:46.999 --> 01:06:48.836
It's my birthday, bitch!

01:06:48.938 --> 01:06:51.270
It's my birthday,
and I'm getting candy!

01:06:54.407 --> 01:06:57.437
And give me some goddamn
lottery tickets, too.

01:06:57.539 --> 01:06:59.709
Put the...
Put the candy... Fuck.

01:06:59.812 --> 01:07:01.348
[exclaims]

01:07:01.451 --> 01:07:03.348
[cackling]

01:07:06.150 --> 01:07:08.452
[dramatic music playing]

01:07:10.186 --> 01:07:12.126
Hey! Hey! Hey! Hey!

01:07:17.667 --> 01:07:19.527
[dramatic music continues]

01:07:19.629 --> 01:07:22.598
Did you get it? Did you get it?
Thank you.

01:07:24.271 --> 01:07:27.706
Hey! Hey, hey! Where is it?
Where is it?

01:07:27.808 --> 01:07:28.773
What the fuck, man?

01:07:28.875 --> 01:07:30.336
Where'd you put it?

01:07:30.438 --> 01:07:32.245
[dramatic music continues]

01:07:34.881 --> 01:07:36.111
[music fades out]

01:07:36.213 --> 01:07:38.015
That's him right there.

01:07:38.118 --> 01:07:41.248
-Security guard.
-[Ryan] No shit.

01:07:41.350 --> 01:07:43.018
It's this guy right here.

01:07:43.854 --> 01:07:46.155
I'm sitting there, I'm watching
the guy in the fucking suit.

01:07:46.257 --> 01:07:47.991
And this bastard is right there.

01:07:48.093 --> 01:07:49.255
Yeah, you remember him?

01:07:49.357 --> 01:07:51.959
[cellphone ringing]

01:07:52.662 --> 01:07:54.935
-Yeah.
-[operator]<i> A person is calling</i>

01:07:55.037 --> 01:07:57.131
<i> through</i>
<i> the Tri-State Relay Service.</i>

01:07:57.700 --> 01:07:59.699
<i> Have you received a call</i>
<i> from us before?</i>

01:07:59.802 --> 01:08:02.770
Yes, we have.
Just give me one second, please.

01:08:03.779 --> 01:08:07.577
Hey, yo. Hey, hey. TTY.

01:08:08.585 --> 01:08:09.744
[Dawson grunts]

01:08:12.381 --> 01:08:13.880
Yeah. I'm here. Go ahead.

01:08:13.982 --> 01:08:17.354
<i> "We've got 40 copies,</i>
<i>including the missing appendix,</i>

01:08:17.456 --> 01:08:19.726
ready to go to spread across
the mainstream

01:08:19.828 --> 01:08:21.360
and alternative media.

01:08:21.462 --> 01:08:24.764
<i> You agreed to stop following</i>
<i> and harassing her."</i>

01:08:24.866 --> 01:08:26.266
She was in Times Square

01:08:26.368 --> 01:08:28.830
with a document that contains
sensitive material.

01:08:28.932 --> 01:08:31.900
<i> You wouldn't know that</i>
<i> if you weren't following her.</i>

01:08:32.436 --> 01:08:34.272
<i> Do you want us to go public?"</i>

01:08:34.375 --> 01:08:36.441
We apologize. We're sorry.
We made a mistake.

01:08:36.543 --> 01:08:39.013
And we'll do exactly as you say
from now on. Go ahead.

01:08:39.116 --> 01:08:41.311
<i> "The handover will be</i>
<i> between our client</i>

01:08:41.413 --> 01:08:44.449
<i> and your CEO, Franklin,</i>
<i> in person,</i>

01:08:44.551 --> 01:08:49.187
<i>in a public place of our choice</i>
<i> at 7 p.m. on Thursday."</i>

01:08:49.289 --> 01:08:51.126
[Dawson]
<i> Mr. Franklin is out of town.</i>

01:08:51.958 --> 01:08:53.990
Well, get him back.

01:08:54.092 --> 01:08:55.455
"Ask him to return."

01:08:55.557 --> 01:08:56.756
Oh, yeah. I'll try my best.

01:08:56.858 --> 01:08:58.800
Thursday is the day before
the SEC filing.

01:08:58.902 --> 01:09:00.427
That's cutting it close.
Go ahead.

01:09:00.529 --> 01:09:02.131
<i> "You'd better make it work."</i>

01:09:02.233 --> 01:09:03.132
<i> Your caller has hung up.</i>

01:09:03.234 --> 01:09:04.803
<i> Thank you for using--</i>

01:09:04.905 --> 01:09:06.003
[disconnect tone]

01:09:06.105 --> 01:09:08.440
That's it. We got our guy.

01:09:09.271 --> 01:09:10.272
That's him.

01:09:10.774 --> 01:09:12.940
We'll get him to our friends
at a fusion center.

01:09:13.042 --> 01:09:15.379
For facial recognition?
I don't think it's good enough.

01:09:15.481 --> 01:09:17.277
That's the best frame
of his face we have.

01:09:17.379 --> 01:09:20.155
[cell phone ringing]

01:09:22.320 --> 01:09:23.686
[cell phone continues ringing]

01:09:26.995 --> 01:09:28.763
Your call is now connected.

01:09:28.865 --> 01:09:31.430
Are you all right? Go ahead.

01:09:35.165 --> 01:09:36.600
Uh, are you th--

01:09:37.640 --> 01:09:38.767
Are you there?

01:09:41.643 --> 01:09:43.211
Hello?

01:09:50.882 --> 01:09:54.286
<i> "We have it. We're setting</i>
<i> the exchange for Thursday.</i>

01:09:54.388 --> 01:09:57.087
<i> Until then,</i>
<i> you'll call each day once</i>

01:09:57.189 --> 01:09:58.253
<i> and leave a message.</i>

01:09:58.789 --> 01:10:02.288
You'll say, 'All right,'
or you'll say, 'Weather.'

01:10:02.390 --> 01:10:03.664
Nothing more.

01:10:04.300 --> 01:10:06.364
<i> You'll follow instructions</i>
<i> because this time,</i>

01:10:06.466 --> 01:10:10.238
<i> we will walk away.</i>
<i> Do you understand?"</i>

01:10:10.902 --> 01:10:11.899
Yes.

01:10:13.769 --> 01:10:16.343
-Go ahead.
<i> -Your caller has hung up.</i>

01:10:16.445 --> 01:10:19.010
<i> Thank you for using</i>
<i> the Tri-State Relay Service.</i>

01:10:19.112 --> 01:10:20.648
<i> Have a wonderful night.</i>

01:10:20.750 --> 01:10:21.744
[call disconnects]

01:10:34.491 --> 01:10:37.331
[siren wailing in distance]

01:10:40.330 --> 01:10:42.534
[indistinct chatter]

01:10:44.569 --> 01:10:49.310
Hey. Um, I'd like
to book a table, please.

01:10:52.245 --> 01:10:53.775
We tracked it as far as Bell.

01:10:53.877 --> 01:10:56.881
There's a national distribution
center there.

01:10:56.983 --> 01:10:58.286
Then we lost it.

01:10:59.449 --> 01:11:01.220
Will the signal come back?

01:11:01.322 --> 01:11:03.920
[Lee]
There were no backup batteries.

01:11:04.556 --> 01:11:05.926
[Dawson]
Where's it gonna go from there?

01:11:06.029 --> 01:11:08.021
It could literally be anywhere.

01:11:09.393 --> 01:11:11.596
[tense music playing]

01:11:30.951 --> 01:11:32.287
All right.

01:11:38.653 --> 01:11:39.987
[on message]<i> All right.</i>

01:11:43.162 --> 01:11:44.728
[voice mail beeps]

01:11:46.695 --> 01:11:48.768
[on message]<i> It's Hoffman.</i>

01:11:49.571 --> 01:11:51.699
<i> I've been checking</i>
<i> the obituaries of the towns</i>

01:11:51.801 --> 01:11:54.408
<i> that were part of</i>
<i> Optimo's trials.</i>

01:11:55.409 --> 01:11:58.841
<i> Healthy young people</i>
<i> suddenly dying.</i>

01:12:00.543 --> 01:12:02.482
<i> How many more are there?</i>

01:12:03.551 --> 01:12:06.282
<i> We all knew</i>
<i> the trials were inadequate.</i>

01:12:06.985 --> 01:12:10.754
<i> They said things were safe</i>
<i> way before we knew enough.</i>

01:12:11.790 --> 01:12:14.824
<i> You know how widely</i>
<i> it was distributed.</i>

01:12:16.399 --> 01:12:19.092
<i> Millions of people</i>
<i> will have been affected,</i>

01:12:20.200 --> 01:12:22.330
<i> but Optimo will deny it.</i>

01:12:22.933 --> 01:12:25.802
<i>I had a chance to do something,</i>
<i> and I blew it.</i>

01:12:27.736 --> 01:12:29.707
<i> I've got blood on my hands.</i>

01:12:31.511 --> 01:12:34.580
<i> It's not your fault.</i>
<i> You helped me.</i>

01:12:36.044 --> 01:12:39.684
<i> Thank you.</i>
<i> I won't bother you again.</i>

01:12:40.516 --> 01:12:42.082
[voice mail beeps]

01:12:53.102 --> 01:12:55.131
I'm Jon, and I'm an alcoholic.

01:12:55.233 --> 01:12:56.696
[all] Hi, Jon.

01:12:57.232 --> 01:13:01.035
Growing up Muslim, you're not
supposed to drink at all.

01:13:02.074 --> 01:13:04.244
I, uh...

01:13:04.346 --> 01:13:06.843
So, I grew up Muslim
in New York...

01:13:08.114 --> 01:13:09.549
post 9/11.

01:13:10.116 --> 01:13:11.513
It was crazy.

01:13:11.882 --> 01:13:15.819
I figured drinking
would help me to fit in

01:13:16.719 --> 01:13:18.888
and just connect to people more.

01:13:20.293 --> 01:13:22.864
And it did, a little.

01:13:23.500 --> 01:13:26.265
Didn't stop me getting
my ass kicked all the time.

01:13:26.634 --> 01:13:31.406
But when that happened,
it would help me go numb.

01:13:32.206 --> 01:13:34.208
So, either way, it helped.

01:13:34.310 --> 01:13:37.537
And then I got a job
on Wall Street.

01:13:37.639 --> 01:13:39.178
It was intense.

01:13:39.280 --> 01:13:41.114
Drinking was part of fitting in.

01:13:41.216 --> 01:13:42.481
And it was a way of dealing

01:13:42.583 --> 01:13:45.646
with pressure to meet
these crazy targets.

01:13:45.749 --> 01:13:47.752
There was no way
of meeting them.

01:13:48.685 --> 01:13:51.024
Not without bending the rules

01:13:51.126 --> 01:13:52.590
and screwing people over.

01:13:52.692 --> 01:13:54.722
Much as I wanted to be
a part of something,

01:13:54.824 --> 01:13:56.296
I didn't wanna be
a part of that.

01:13:56.398 --> 01:13:59.594
So, I started
gathering information,

01:13:59.696 --> 01:14:02.536
and I took it to my superiors.

01:14:03.336 --> 01:14:04.901
They took a look at it.

01:14:07.176 --> 01:14:09.103
And nothing really happened.

01:14:10.443 --> 01:14:13.613
The investigation was one-sided.

01:14:15.647 --> 01:14:17.584
It all blew over.
And when it did,

01:14:17.686 --> 01:14:20.517
people I had known a long time
turned their backs on me,

01:14:20.619 --> 01:14:23.516
started spreading rumors
about me.

01:14:24.252 --> 01:14:29.197
You know, questioning my sanity
and my integrity.

01:14:29.299 --> 01:14:35.596
And I started to become,
uh, paranoid

01:14:35.698 --> 01:14:39.567
and aggressive and drunk.

01:14:40.303 --> 01:14:43.373
By the time they came to me
with this severance package,

01:14:43.475 --> 01:14:45.139
it was tied to an NDA.

01:14:47.214 --> 01:14:48.780
I was relieved.

01:14:50.447 --> 01:14:51.952
So, I, uh...

01:14:52.054 --> 01:14:53.680
I took the money.

01:14:53.782 --> 01:14:55.386
I kept my mouth shut,

01:14:55.488 --> 01:14:57.317
poured it all down my throat.

01:14:57.419 --> 01:15:02.963
But I still carry a lot of guilt
and shame about that time.

01:15:03.399 --> 01:15:05.425
And I keep thinking
I was a coward.

01:15:05.728 --> 01:15:08.134
And I was weak. I was.

01:15:08.536 --> 01:15:10.964
I got a call from someone
last night,

01:15:11.066 --> 01:15:15.510
and he just sounded
so... lost...

01:15:17.210 --> 01:15:18.876
and broken.

01:15:20.176 --> 01:15:23.914
And I don't think
he's gonna make it, honestly.

01:15:26.454 --> 01:15:28.523
I don't wanna end up like that.

01:15:36.229 --> 01:15:37.730
Thank you, Wash.

01:15:38.795 --> 01:15:41.734
[suspenseful music playing]

01:15:58.283 --> 01:16:00.284
[buzzing]

01:16:00.386 --> 01:16:01.721
[cellphone ringing]

01:16:07.390 --> 01:16:10.730
"The original copy of the report
is waiting under your name

01:16:10.832 --> 01:16:14.035
<i> in General Delivery at</i>
<i> the main post office on 8th.</i>

01:16:14.504 --> 01:16:15.965
<i> A table is booked</i>
<i> for Adam Franklin</i>

01:16:16.067 --> 01:16:18.835
<i> at Gaia & Loki restaurant</i>
<i> at 7 p.m. tonight.</i>

01:16:18.937 --> 01:16:20.841
<i> Take a taxi there</i>
<i> and make it wait.</i>

01:16:20.943 --> 01:16:23.708
<i> Bring the report in the yellow</i>
<i> marked phone you were sent.</i>

01:16:23.810 --> 01:16:25.511
<i> When he arrives,</i>
<i> hand him the documents,</i>

01:16:25.613 --> 01:16:26.941
<i> take a picture</i>
<i> of the two of you,</i>

01:16:27.043 --> 01:16:29.846
<i> get back in the taxi</i>
<i> and head uptown.</i>

01:16:29.949 --> 01:16:32.580
<i> You will receive</i>
<i> further instructions then.</i>

01:16:32.682 --> 01:16:34.120
Do you understand?"

01:16:34.222 --> 01:16:36.557
Yes, I do. Go ahead.

01:16:36.659 --> 01:16:38.351
<i> Your caller has hung up.</i>
<i> Thank you for using</i>

01:16:38.453 --> 01:16:41.629
<i> the Tri-State Relay Service.</i>
<i> Have a wonderful day.</i>

01:16:47.536 --> 01:16:49.065
"Mr. Franklin
must attend in person,

01:16:49.167 --> 01:16:51.067
and our client will need
to take a photograph with him.

01:16:51.169 --> 01:16:53.440
<i> She will return the original</i>
<i> copy of the report,</i>

01:16:53.542 --> 01:16:54.970
<i> and we will keep</i>
<i> a single safety copy</i>

01:16:55.072 --> 01:16:57.006
<i> to ensure everyone</i>
<i> sticks to the deal."</i>

01:16:57.108 --> 01:16:58.844
<i> Your caller has hung up.</i>
<i> Thank you for using</i>

01:16:58.946 --> 01:17:01.649
<i> the Tri-State Relay Service.</i>
<i> Have a wonderful--</i>

01:17:06.915 --> 01:17:09.118
[dramatic music playing]

01:17:16.291 --> 01:17:18.358
[bartender] Can I get you
another club soda?

01:17:19.365 --> 01:17:20.431
No. I'm good.

01:17:20.533 --> 01:17:21.966
-Okay.
-Thank you.

01:17:24.735 --> 01:17:26.971
[dramatic music continues]

01:17:31.310 --> 01:17:33.076
[beeping]

01:17:59.267 --> 01:18:01.237
[automated voice]
<i> ...one new message.</i>

01:18:01.339 --> 01:18:04.544
[Sarah on message]<i> Weather.</i>
<i> I know I should have called.</i>

01:18:04.646 --> 01:18:06.675
<i> You don't have to worry.</i>
<i> I'm okay.</i>

01:18:06.777 --> 01:18:07.842
<i> They know who you are.</i>

01:18:07.944 --> 01:18:09.517
<i> They said facial recognition</i>

01:18:09.619 --> 01:18:11.783
<i> got a positive ID of you</i>
<i> in Times Square.</i>

01:18:11.885 --> 01:18:15.382
<i> They told me your name.</i>
<i> James Keaton.</i>

01:18:15.484 --> 01:18:18.659
<i> You're in big danger, James.</i>
<i> This is my fault.</i>

01:18:18.761 --> 01:18:20.222
<i> You've got to get out of here</i>
<i> and stay away.</i>

01:18:20.324 --> 01:18:22.662
-No, no, no, no, no.
<i> -I screwed up in Times Square,</i>

01:18:22.764 --> 01:18:24.727
<i> so I'm gonna do</i>
<i> this handover myself.</i>

01:18:24.829 --> 01:18:26.798
-Fuck!
<i> -There's a concert</i>

01:18:26.900 --> 01:18:29.636
<i> of Schubert's</i>
Piano Trios<i> at town hall.</i>

01:18:29.739 --> 01:18:31.901
<i> It's public,</i>
<i> like you said it should be.</i>

01:18:32.003 --> 01:18:33.602
-Fuck!
<i> -They told me not to tell you,</i>

01:18:33.704 --> 01:18:36.236
<i> but I needed to.</i>

01:18:36.338 --> 01:18:38.405
<i> And to thank you</i>
<i> for looking after me.</i>

01:18:39.612 --> 01:18:41.577
<i> Goodbye, James. Be safe.</i>

01:18:41.679 --> 01:18:43.883
[car horns honking]

01:18:54.692 --> 01:18:56.126
Let me get a ticket.

01:18:57.463 --> 01:18:58.559
Here you are.

01:18:59.062 --> 01:19:00.727
-Keep the change.
-Thank you.

01:19:00.829 --> 01:19:01.764
[detector beeps]

01:19:01.866 --> 01:19:04.035
[classical music playing nearby]

01:19:06.704 --> 01:19:08.708
Whoa, what is that?

01:19:08.811 --> 01:19:10.478
It's a hearing-assisted device
for the deaf.

01:19:10.580 --> 01:19:12.142
All right.
Well, you gotta check it.

01:19:15.979 --> 01:19:18.181
[classical music continues]

01:20:13.935 --> 01:20:16.173
[line ringing]

01:20:43.701 --> 01:20:45.598
[line ringing]

01:21:11.928 --> 01:21:14.630
[alarm blaring]

01:21:14.732 --> 01:21:15.595
[music stops]

01:21:18.837 --> 01:21:20.472
[alarm continues blaring]

01:21:20.574 --> 01:21:22.536
[audience murmuring]

01:21:57.213 --> 01:21:58.374
[groans]

01:21:59.744 --> 01:22:00.541
[crowd gasps]

01:22:02.212 --> 01:22:04.280
It's me. It's me.
Credit or debit.

01:22:04.382 --> 01:22:06.420
It's a trap. They're coming
to get you. Come on.

01:22:06.522 --> 01:22:08.422
[dramatic music playing]

01:22:08.524 --> 01:22:10.683
Excuse me. Excuse me.

01:22:20.734 --> 01:22:22.902
[dramatic music continues]

01:22:23.005 --> 01:22:24.868
-[alarm continues blaring]
-Move, move, move!

01:22:24.971 --> 01:22:27.101
-[siren wailing]
-Put this on.

01:22:27.203 --> 01:22:28.709
Put this on. Take this off.

01:22:28.811 --> 01:22:30.805
Did you give it to them?
The report.

01:22:30.907 --> 01:22:32.208
-No.
-Good.

01:22:32.310 --> 01:22:33.877
Our threat to go public
has to feel real.

01:22:33.980 --> 01:22:35.277
It's the only leverage you got.

01:22:35.613 --> 01:22:38.116
Take the train to Poughkeepsie.
You're gonna pay in cash.

01:22:38.218 --> 01:22:40.715
When you get there,
you go to the Grand Hotel.

01:22:40.817 --> 01:22:43.583
You book under your own name,
but you misspell it, all right?

01:22:43.685 --> 01:22:45.756
I gotta go back to the apartment
and get my stuff.

01:22:45.858 --> 01:22:48.090
No, you don't. You can't.

01:22:48.192 --> 01:22:49.825
How did they get
in touch with you?

01:22:50.261 --> 01:22:52.065
They, uh...
They rang the intercom.

01:22:54.228 --> 01:22:55.567
Did they hurt you?

01:22:55.669 --> 01:22:57.236
-No.
-Okay, good.

01:22:57.338 --> 01:22:59.133
When you get there, call me
and let me know you're okay.

01:22:59.235 --> 01:23:00.501
I'm gonna call you right ba--

01:23:00.603 --> 01:23:03.107
We're gonna contact you
with a P.O. Box number.

01:23:03.210 --> 01:23:05.171
All right? You're gonna
have to remember it.

01:23:05.273 --> 01:23:06.842
Will you just tell me?

01:23:07.412 --> 01:23:09.275
I gotta protect you
while you're traveling.

01:23:09.844 --> 01:23:13.081
You go to the main post office,
ask for an envelope.

01:23:13.183 --> 01:23:14.787
It's got a P.O. Box key in it

01:23:14.889 --> 01:23:16.321
and the rest
of the instructions.

01:23:16.423 --> 01:23:17.486
Yo!

01:23:18.624 --> 01:23:19.554
Let's go.

01:23:20.758 --> 01:23:21.754
Here.

01:23:26.261 --> 01:23:27.727
Grand Central. Let's go.

01:23:37.413 --> 01:23:38.375
You're okay.

01:23:41.750 --> 01:23:43.446
-You got the papers?
-Yeah.

01:23:44.786 --> 01:23:46.348
From now on, it's cash only.

01:23:46.450 --> 01:23:48.814
Use a card,
they're gonna trace you. ID.

01:23:48.916 --> 01:23:51.623
You got a new one waiting
for you at the post office.

01:23:51.725 --> 01:23:53.654
Stop. Please stop.

01:23:56.325 --> 01:23:58.329
Why did you do this for me?

01:24:01.899 --> 01:24:03.367
It's my job.

01:24:05.903 --> 01:24:09.241
Was that all?

01:24:14.008 --> 01:24:17.645
You know, you're exactly and not
at all what I imagined, James.

01:24:19.654 --> 01:24:21.180
That's not my name.

01:24:21.282 --> 01:24:23.123
They lied to you.

01:24:28.058 --> 01:24:29.723
What is your name?

01:24:41.410 --> 01:24:42.538
It's Ash.

01:24:44.578 --> 01:24:45.772
Ashraf.

01:24:51.585 --> 01:24:52.886
[scoffs]

01:24:52.988 --> 01:24:55.082
Am I your worst client ever,
Ashraf?

01:24:55.184 --> 01:24:57.388
[chuckles] Maybe.

01:25:09.800 --> 01:25:10.830
Hey.

01:25:17.240 --> 01:25:19.707
You're gonna be all right.

01:25:24.984 --> 01:25:26.681
Come with me, Ashraf.

01:25:30.822 --> 01:25:32.192
I can't.

01:25:44.000 --> 01:25:45.304
Goodbye.

01:25:49.940 --> 01:25:51.244
Keep it.

01:26:05.759 --> 01:26:07.293
Don't look back.

01:26:31.820 --> 01:26:33.814
[wistful music playing]

01:26:35.485 --> 01:26:37.719
[man speaking indistinctly
over PA]

01:27:03.719 --> 01:27:04.713
[music fades out]

01:27:14.225 --> 01:27:16.461
[tense music playing]

01:27:27.369 --> 01:27:28.671
[cellphone ringing]

01:27:40.217 --> 01:27:41.722
"What was your plan?

01:27:41.824 --> 01:27:43.217
<i> That I was bluffing?</i>

01:27:43.686 --> 01:27:45.319
<i> I'll make sure</i>
<i> you never find her.</i>

01:27:45.421 --> 01:27:47.657
<i> She's gone and so am I."</i>

01:27:49.557 --> 01:27:50.792
[teletype disconnects]

01:27:52.494 --> 01:27:53.993
<i> Your caller has hung up.</i>

01:27:54.095 --> 01:27:56.130
<i> Thank you for using</i>
<i> the Tri-State Relay Service.</i>

01:27:56.232 --> 01:27:57.097
<i> Have a won--</i>

01:27:57.199 --> 01:27:58.404
[sighs]

01:28:01.743 --> 01:28:02.837
Thank you.

01:28:05.407 --> 01:28:07.809
[cellphone buzzes]

01:28:10.714 --> 01:28:12.646
Sarah, you can't use this phone.
All right?

01:28:12.748 --> 01:28:14.721
You got to get rid of it
right away.

01:28:15.257 --> 01:28:17.018
[Dawson]<i> Glad to finally</i>
<i> hear your voice.</i>

01:28:17.120 --> 01:28:20.323
<i>We're getting bored of speaking</i>
<i> to this fucking relay service.</i>

01:28:20.759 --> 01:28:23.423
<i> This little phone has been</i>
<i> very useful. Thank you.</i>

01:28:23.525 --> 01:28:24.991
<i> I'll get her for you.</i>

01:28:27.701 --> 01:28:28.894
[Sarah]<i> Don't do what they say.</i>
<i> They were tracking me.</i>

01:28:28.996 --> 01:28:30.597
Sarah, listen to me.
You gotta stay calm.

01:28:30.699 --> 01:28:32.037
<i> -It's my fault.</i>
-Listen to me.

01:28:32.139 --> 01:28:33.437
We're gonna figure this out.

01:28:33.539 --> 01:28:35.204
-Just stay calm for me.
<i> -Just walk away.</i>

01:28:35.306 --> 01:28:36.475
[Dawson]<i> Give it here.</i>

01:28:38.477 --> 01:28:40.377
<i> You're going to do what</i>
<i> we say now.</i>

01:28:40.479 --> 01:28:42.811
<i> -You understand?</i>
-Listen, let her go.

01:28:42.913 --> 01:28:45.883
All right? The documents
are going out, all of them.

01:28:46.419 --> 01:28:47.913
-You hear me?
<i> -And then what, huh?</i>

01:28:48.282 --> 01:28:50.649
<i> The idea of journalists or</i>
<i> their readers actually caring,</i>

01:28:50.752 --> 01:28:52.554
<i> it's a cute, liberal fantasy.</i>

01:28:52.656 --> 01:28:54.325
Most of the media work
with us anyway,

01:28:54.427 --> 01:28:56.196
so they won't publish
in a hurry.

01:28:56.565 --> 01:28:58.963
And that leaves the conspiracy
theorists on social media.

01:28:59.065 --> 01:28:59.966
Good luck with that.

01:29:00.068 --> 01:29:01.200
Guess what. Law enforcement

01:29:01.302 --> 01:29:03.001
is gonna be reading
more closely,

01:29:03.103 --> 01:29:04.464
so don't fucking push me.

01:29:04.566 --> 01:29:06.204
The envelopes are labeled

01:29:06.306 --> 01:29:07.902
-and sealed.
<i> -Here's the deal.</i>

01:29:09.373 --> 01:29:11.078
We're gonna come with you

01:29:11.180 --> 01:29:13.342
to wherever
you keep your documents,

01:29:13.911 --> 01:29:15.779
and you're gonna give us
all the copies of the report,

01:29:15.881 --> 01:29:17.877
including your safety copy,
and we'll let her go unharmed.

01:29:17.979 --> 01:29:19.416
<i> And you, too,</i>
<i> if you behave yourself.</i>

01:29:19.518 --> 01:29:21.087
You gotta be
out your fucking mind.

01:29:21.189 --> 01:29:22.715
I have other clients
to consider.

01:29:22.817 --> 01:29:24.352
You really think
you have a choice?

01:29:24.454 --> 01:29:25.518
<i> ♪ It's just a game ♪</i>

01:29:25.620 --> 01:29:27.124
<i> ♪ It's just a game ♪</i>

01:29:27.226 --> 01:29:28.356
<i> ♪ It's just a game ♪</i>

01:29:28.458 --> 01:29:29.896
<i> ♪ It's just a game ♪</i>

01:29:29.998 --> 01:29:31.260
<i> ♪ It's just a game ♪</i>

01:29:31.362 --> 01:29:32.491
<i> ♪ It's just a game ♪</i>

01:29:32.593 --> 01:29:33.999
<i> ♪ It's just... ♪</i>

01:29:34.101 --> 01:29:36.095
[dramatic music playing]

01:30:25.381 --> 01:30:27.553
[chuckling]

01:30:54.883 --> 01:30:57.110
[line ringing]

01:30:59.218 --> 01:31:00.487
[Dawson]<i> Yeah?</i>

01:31:01.418 --> 01:31:02.819
Yeah, I'll do it.

01:31:04.053 --> 01:31:05.817
I'll take you
to all the records. I'll do it.

01:31:05.920 --> 01:31:07.923
<i> That's good. That's very good.</i>

01:31:08.025 --> 01:31:10.695
<i> Dawn tomorrow, you come</i>
<i> to your client's apartment.</i>

01:32:10.887 --> 01:32:12.691
-[electricity crackling]
-[Ash groans]

01:32:16.359 --> 01:32:17.157
[gasps]

01:32:17.899 --> 01:32:18.763
[grunts]

01:32:20.001 --> 01:32:21.262
Sarah, you okay?

01:32:21.364 --> 01:32:22.261
I'm fine.

01:32:25.500 --> 01:32:27.007
[groans]

01:32:27.109 --> 01:32:28.438
Where's the documents?

01:32:28.540 --> 01:32:30.269
You let her go, I'll tell you.

01:32:32.441 --> 01:32:33.373
[groans]

01:32:33.475 --> 01:32:35.148
Stop.

01:32:35.650 --> 01:32:37.649
You want the documents,
you need us both alive.

01:32:37.751 --> 01:32:40.279
So, why don't you let her go,
and we'll talk.

01:32:41.288 --> 01:32:42.820
Don't really need her.

01:32:43.387 --> 01:32:44.890
Hey! Easy.

01:32:44.992 --> 01:32:46.391
[wails]

01:32:46.493 --> 01:32:47.954
-Hey!
-Where are the documents?

01:32:48.056 --> 01:32:50.694
10001 South Second Street,
Newark.

01:32:50.796 --> 01:32:53.963
[Lee] Newark.
10001 South Second Street.

01:32:55.566 --> 01:32:57.663
He likes you. [chuckles]

01:32:57.765 --> 01:32:59.498
[tires screeching]

01:32:59.600 --> 01:33:00.607
[grunts]

01:33:03.406 --> 01:33:04.877
[groans]

01:33:04.980 --> 01:33:06.107
[grunting]

01:33:07.314 --> 01:33:09.649
Oh, you motherfucker!

01:33:13.154 --> 01:33:14.251
[grunts then yells]

01:33:14.353 --> 01:33:16.682
[car horn honking]

01:33:16.784 --> 01:33:18.350
[both grunting]

01:33:26.531 --> 01:33:28.063
[soft tense music playing]

01:33:35.306 --> 01:33:36.335
[groans]

01:33:39.707 --> 01:33:42.047
[Ash groaning]

01:33:42.416 --> 01:33:43.914
[Dawson] Oh, you motherfucker.

01:33:45.913 --> 01:33:48.116
[tense music continues]

01:33:51.058 --> 01:33:51.724
Stop.

01:33:57.793 --> 01:33:58.962
[Dawson] Good job, boss.

01:33:59.495 --> 01:34:01.701
[panting]

01:34:04.533 --> 01:34:05.672
[groans]

01:34:17.416 --> 01:34:18.682
What do you want?

01:34:19.084 --> 01:34:22.348
We want your copy of the
Optimo Pharmaceutical report.

01:34:24.392 --> 01:34:27.023
Yeah. This is about Hoffman.

01:34:48.645 --> 01:34:50.114
Here, here. Here.

01:34:50.216 --> 01:34:51.451
[groans]

01:34:51.553 --> 01:34:53.214
[Dawson] Unlock it.
Okay, come on.

01:34:54.517 --> 01:34:55.315
Come on.

01:35:00.591 --> 01:35:02.589
This one? Come here.

01:35:02.691 --> 01:35:03.996
[Ash groans]

01:35:04.098 --> 01:35:05.424
Come on.

01:35:12.568 --> 01:35:13.666
Come on.

01:35:13.768 --> 01:35:14.568
[Ash grunts]

01:35:14.670 --> 01:35:16.774
This? Huh? What?

01:35:16.876 --> 01:35:18.977
You got to untie my hands
so I can reach it.

01:35:19.079 --> 01:35:22.278
Legs, too. I got two more alarms
to turn off when I get in.

01:35:23.214 --> 01:35:26.213
I'll cut them. You stabbed me
in the motherfucking leg.

01:35:26.315 --> 01:35:28.920
I'll put this
in your fucking ribs, trust me.

01:35:33.954 --> 01:35:35.762
Come on, get to it.

01:35:39.827 --> 01:35:40.992
[keypad beeping]

01:35:41.094 --> 01:35:42.468
-[error beep]
-Fuck!

01:35:42.804 --> 01:35:45.365
Give me a sec.
I just gotta concentrate, okay?

01:35:47.574 --> 01:35:49.743
[Dawson] Get to it. Come on.

01:35:50.805 --> 01:35:53.079
[keypad beeping]

01:35:53.181 --> 01:35:53.945
[error beep]

01:35:55.008 --> 01:35:56.074
Nothing's happening.

01:35:56.176 --> 01:35:57.842
I'm gonna fucking shoot him.

01:35:57.944 --> 01:35:59.786
[keypad beeping]

01:36:02.017 --> 01:36:04.516
What the fuck is that? Hey!

01:36:05.691 --> 01:36:07.156
[suspenseful music playing]

01:36:11.760 --> 01:36:13.096
[Ash grunts]

01:36:30.879 --> 01:36:31.950
[Dawson whistles]

01:36:33.983 --> 01:36:36.218
[suspenseful music continues]

01:36:46.927 --> 01:36:47.966
[Ryan groans]

01:36:48.697 --> 01:36:50.166
[groans]

01:36:51.098 --> 01:36:53.334
[dramatic music playing]

01:37:11.890 --> 01:37:13.457
-I need a gun.
-Don't kill him.

01:37:13.559 --> 01:37:14.492
We need the code.

01:37:14.594 --> 01:37:16.588
[dramatic music continues]

01:37:19.234 --> 01:37:21.835
[gunshots]

01:37:28.941 --> 01:37:31.075
-[car horn honks]
-[tires screeching]

01:37:33.776 --> 01:37:35.244
[groaning]

01:37:49.626 --> 01:37:50.523
[gunshot]

01:38:06.141 --> 01:38:08.013
He's crossing the tracks. Go!

01:38:09.077 --> 01:38:11.313
[dramatic music continues]

01:38:28.602 --> 01:38:30.662
[music turns suspenseful]

01:39:09.904 --> 01:39:11.043
[grunts]

01:39:18.717 --> 01:39:20.453
He's over here!

01:39:20.555 --> 01:39:22.818
Stay with him. Hold him!

01:39:22.920 --> 01:39:24.518
[music turns dramatic]

01:39:50.747 --> 01:39:52.018
[gunshot]

01:40:11.070 --> 01:40:13.336
Give me the code,
and I'll let you go.

01:40:23.715 --> 01:40:25.043
I'll do it.

01:40:25.145 --> 01:40:26.250
[music stops]

01:40:43.030 --> 01:40:44.400
Do it.

01:40:49.774 --> 01:40:50.637
[sirens wailing]

01:41:00.882 --> 01:41:02.484
No.

01:41:03.922 --> 01:41:06.125
[somber music playing]

01:41:08.928 --> 01:41:10.058
[officer 1] Put your hands up!

01:41:10.160 --> 01:41:11.692
Hands where I can see them.

01:41:12.161 --> 01:41:14.094
[indistinct radio chatter]

01:41:14.196 --> 01:41:15.329
[somber music continues]

01:41:15.431 --> 01:41:17.136
[officer 2]
Okay, stay right there.

01:41:21.203 --> 01:41:22.906
Stay calm. Stay calm.

01:41:23.008 --> 01:41:25.240
[officers shouting indistinctly]

01:41:25.342 --> 01:41:26.975
[officer 1]
Let me see your hands!

01:41:27.077 --> 01:41:28.774
-Easy, okay?
-Shut up!

01:41:37.022 --> 01:41:38.751
Come on. In the car. Come on.

01:41:44.796 --> 01:41:45.964
What is this?

01:41:46.366 --> 01:41:49.365
I got documents that show
Optimo Pharmaceutical's products

01:41:49.467 --> 01:41:51.233
have adverse effects,
and they knew about it.

01:41:51.335 --> 01:41:52.638
They tried to cover up
the evidence.

01:41:52.740 --> 01:41:54.199
I got the internal memos.

01:41:54.301 --> 01:41:55.068
I got the e-mails.

01:41:55.170 --> 01:41:56.135
I got everything.

01:41:56.237 --> 01:41:57.271
Why do you have it?

01:41:57.807 --> 01:42:00.843
This is what I do. I help people
who find things like this.

01:42:01.412 --> 01:42:02.841
Who see things maybe
they shouldn't have,

01:42:02.943 --> 01:42:05.347
who should have looked
the other way, but they can't.

01:42:05.449 --> 01:42:08.253
Now I gotta turn it over
to somebody I trust.

01:42:13.626 --> 01:42:14.655
Yeah.

01:42:18.293 --> 01:42:20.496
[somber music continues]

01:42:55.098 --> 01:42:56.862
[music fades out]

01:43:20.091 --> 01:43:21.793
It's a little heavy there.

01:43:21.895 --> 01:43:22.888
-Thank you.
-Okay.

01:43:25.097 --> 01:43:27.299
[soft dramatic music playing]

01:44:26.958 --> 01:44:28.954
[bell ringing]

01:44:31.931 --> 01:44:34.025
[blows whistle]

01:45:09.068 --> 01:45:11.700
[ominous music playing]

01:45:34.191 --> 01:45:36.395
[inaudible dialogue]

01:45:45.037 --> 01:45:47.032
[train horn blaring]

01:46:00.880 --> 01:46:03.081
[Karen Marks's "Cold Café"
playing]

01:46:18.973 --> 01:46:21.402
<i> ♪ On the esplanade ♪</i>

01:46:21.504 --> 01:46:25.539
<i> ♪ My coffee's gone cold ♪</i>

01:46:25.641 --> 01:46:28.777
<i> ♪ I won't forget the sounds ♪</i>

01:46:30.346 --> 01:46:32.814
<i> ♪ You left me ♪</i>

01:46:34.714 --> 01:46:37.956
<i> ♪ Love and television ♪</i>

01:46:38.058 --> 01:46:40.691
<i> ♪ Don't give it a name ♪</i>

01:46:41.127 --> 01:46:43.863
<i> ♪ Take it anyway ♪</i>

01:46:44.332 --> 01:46:49.900
<i> ♪ There's no shelter</i>
<i> In my life ♪</i>

01:46:50.235 --> 01:46:52.931
<i> ♪ Your eyes in mine ♪</i>

01:46:53.033 --> 01:46:58.037
<i> ♪ Smoke in our mouths</i>
<i> Till morning ♪</i>

01:46:59.608 --> 01:47:03.079
♪<i> Your words in my head</i> ♪

01:47:03.414 --> 01:47:08.949
<i> ♪ I don't sleep anymore ♪</i>

01:47:09.650 --> 01:47:12.519
<i> ♪ On the esplanade ♪</i>

